  '=== [诊断] overlay 渲染树 ===': '=== [Diagnostics] overlay render tree ===',
  'A/B 训练日交替': 'Alternating A/B Training Days',
  'BMI 指数': 'BMI',
  'Dart Timer 5秒通知': 'Dart Timer 5-Second Notification',
  'EPOC 不是"练完躺着也瘦"的神话，而是真实的代谢提升效应。但需要配合饮食控制，热量缺口仍是减脂核心': 'EPOC is not the myth of "lie down after your workout and keep burning fat" — it is a real metabolic boost. But it has to be paired with dietary control; a calorie deficit is still the core of fat loss.',
  'EPOC 效应解析': 'Breaking Down the EPOC Effect',
  'GZCLP三层结构：T1主项3×5+（力量）/T2辅助3×10（肌肥大）/T3孤立3×15+（弱项），失败后渐进降次（5→3→2→1）': 'GZCLP\'s three tiers: T1 main lift 3×5+ (strength) / T2 assistance 3×10 (hypertrophy) / T3 isolation 3×15+ (weak points), with progressive rep reduction after failure (5→3→2→1)',
  'HIIT vs LISS 对比': 'HIIT vs LISS',
  'HIIT 不适合所有人。适合：有一定训练基础（3 个月+ 力量训练）、关节健康、无心血管疾病、能承受高强度。不适合：零基础初学者（先建立基础）、关节伤病者（冲击大）、高血压/心脏病患者（心血管压力）、孕妇（避免高强度）。初学者应从 LISS 开始，逐步加入低强度 HIIT（如 30 秒中等强度 + 60 秒恢复），4-8 周后再过渡到标准 HIIT。安全是减脂的前提。': 'HIIT is not for everyone. It suits people who: have a training base (3+ months of strength training), healthy joints, no cardiovascular disease and can tolerate high intensity. It does not suit: complete beginners (build a base first), people with joint injuries (high impact), people with high blood pressure or heart disease (cardiovascular strain) or pregnant women (avoid high intensity). Beginners should start with LISS, then gradually add low-intensity intervals (for example 30 seconds moderate + 60 seconds recovery), and move to standard HIIT after 4-8 weeks. Safety comes before fat loss.',
  'HIIT 力竭状态下动作变形是受伤主因。宁可少做 2 次标准动作，不要多做 2 次变形动作': 'In HIIT, form breakdown at failure is the leading cause of injury. Better to do 2 fewer reps with good form than 2 more with bad form.',
  'HIIT 动作的选择标准': 'How to Choose HIIT Exercises',
  'HIIT 动作选择决定训练效果与安全。四个标准：①多关节——动用大肌群，心率提升快、热量消耗高；②高强度——能在 20-30 秒内将心率拉到 85%+ 最大心率；③安全可控——力竭状态下动作不变形；④可快速切换——动作间过渡不超过 5 秒，维持心率。符合标准的动作：开合跳、高抬腿、波比跳、登山者、战绳、壶铃摆荡、跳箱。不符合：孤立动作（弯举）、复杂技术动作（抓举）、高冲击动作（连续跳深）。': 'Exercise selection determines both the effectiveness and the safety of HIIT. Four criteria: (1) multi-joint — recruits large muscle groups, raising heart rate fast and burning more calories; (2) high intensity — can push heart rate to 85%+ of max within 20-30 seconds; (3) safe and controllable — form holds up at failure; (4) quick to switch — transitions under 5 seconds to keep heart rate up. Exercises that fit: jumping jacks, high knees, burpees, mountain climbers, battle ropes, kettlebell swings, box jumps. Exercises that don\'t: isolation moves (bicep curls), technically complex moves (snatches), high-impact moves (continuous depth jumps).',
  'HIIT 协议选择应根据训练水平。初学者从 40/20 开始，4 周后过渡到 30/30，再 4 周后尝试 Tabata': 'Choose your HIIT protocol based on your training level. Beginners start with 40/20, move to 30/30 after 4 weeks, then try Tabata after another 4 weeks.',
  'HIIT 和 LISS 各有优势，不是替代关系。HIIT 优势：时间短（15-25 分钟 vs 45-60 分钟）、EPOC 高、保留肌肉、提升无氧能力。LISS 优势：关节压力小、恢复快、可每天执行、适合初学者。减脂期最佳策略是结合：每周 2 次 HIIT + 2-3 次 LISS。HIIT 提供代谢刺激和 EPOC，LISS 增加总热量消耗而不影响力量训练恢复。这种组合优于单一形式。': 'HIIT and LISS each have their strengths; neither replaces the other. HIIT\'s advantages: short sessions (15-25 min vs 45-60 min), high EPOC, muscle retention and improved anaerobic capacity. LISS\'s advantages: low joint stress, fast recovery, can be done daily and beginner-friendly. The best fat-loss strategy combines them: 2 HIIT sessions plus 2-3 LISS sessions per week. HIIT provides the metabolic stimulus and EPOC, while LISS raises total calorie burn without hurting recovery from strength training. This combination beats either one alone.',
  'HIIT 和力量训练存在"干扰效应"——过量 HIIT 会通过共享神经恢复资源、累积疲劳、激活 AMPK 通路（抑制 mTOR 肌肥大信号）等方式，抑制力量和肌肥大。研究显示，每周 4 次以上高强度有氧使肌肥大效益降低 30%、力量增长降低 18%。减脂期必须平衡：保留力量训练容量至赤字前 60-80%、HIIT 控制在 2-3 次/周、单次不超过 25 分钟。这种平衡让 HIIT 提供代谢刺激，又不损害力量保留。': 'There is an "interference effect" between HIIT and strength training — too much HIIT suppresses strength and hypertrophy by competing for the same neural recovery resources, accumulating fatigue and activating the AMPK pathway (which inhibits the mTOR hypertrophy signal). Research shows that more than 4 high-intensity cardio sessions per week reduces hypertrophy by 30% and strength gains by 18%. During a cut you have to balance: keep strength training volume at 60-80% of pre-deficit levels, cap HIIT at 2-3 sessions a week, and keep sessions under 25 minutes. That balance lets HIIT deliver a metabolic stimulus without costing you strength.',
  'HIIT 安全核心原则': 'Core HIIT Safety Principles',
  'HIIT 定义：高强度（≥80% 最大心率）+ 间歇恢复的循环训练。\n\nEPOC 效应：运动后过量氧耗，训练后 24-48 小时持续燃脂。\n\n相比 LISS：时间效率高、保留肌肉、代谢提升更显著。': 'HIIT defined: high intensity (≥80% max heart rate) plus interval recovery, repeated in cycles.\n\nEPOC effect: excess post-exercise oxygen consumption keeps you burning fat for 24-48 hours after the session.\n\nVersus LISS: more time-efficient, preserves muscle, and raises metabolism more.',
  'HIIT 对神经系统和结缔组织压力大，频率必须控制。初学者每周 1-2 次、中级 2-3 次、高级 3 次封顶。两次 HIIT 间隔至少 48 小时，让神经系统充分恢复。HIIT 不应连续两天进行，也不应在力量训练次日进行（影响力量恢复）。最佳安排：周一力量、周二 HIIT、周三休息、周四力量、周五 HIIT、周末休息或 LISS。这种安排平衡 HIIT、力量、恢复，是减脂期的黄金组合。': 'HIIT places heavy demands on the nervous system and connective tissue, so frequency has to be controlled: 1-2 sessions a week for beginners, 2-3 for intermediate, 3 maximum for advanced. Leave at least 48 hours between HIIT sessions so the nervous system can fully recover. Never do HIIT two days in a row, or the day after strength training (it hurts strength recovery). A good setup: strength Monday, HIIT Tuesday, rest Wednesday, strength Thursday, HIIT Friday, rest or LISS on the weekend. This balances HIIT, strength and recovery — the gold-standard combination for a cut.',
  'HIIT 常见伤病：膝盖（跳跃落地冲击）、下背（核心不稳代偿）、肩（俯卧撑变形）、跟腱（跳跃落地）。预防：①选择关节友好动作（登山者替代波比跳、椭圆机替代跳绳）；②强化核心（每周 2 次平板支撑训练）；③渐进负荷（不强求高强度协议）；④合适鞋具（避震跑鞋或训练鞋）；⑤充分恢复（48 小时间隔）。出现持续疼痛 3 天以上必须就医，不要"硬扛"。HIIT 是工具，健康是目的。': 'Common HIIT injuries: knees (landing impact from jumps), lower back (core instability compensation), shoulders (push-up form breakdown), Achilles (jump landings). Prevention: (1) choose joint-friendly movements (mountain climbers instead of burpees, elliptical instead of jump rope); (2) strengthen the core (plank training twice a week); (3) progress gradually (don\'t force a high-intensity protocol); (4) wear proper shoes (cushioned running or training shoes); (5) recover fully (48 hours between sessions). If pain lasts more than 3 days, see a doctor — don\'t "push through it". HIIT is the tool; health is the goal.',
  'HIIT 强度高，热身必须充分。标准流程：①5 分钟轻度有氧（开合跳、慢跑）提升体温；②动态拉伸（腿摆、髋部旋转、手臂环绕）3 分钟激活关节；③动作专项激活（深蹲、俯卧撑、波比跳慢速版本）2 分钟预演动作模式。总热身 10 分钟。充分热身将运动损伤风险降低 50% 以上，同时提升 HIIT 表现——冷启动的肌肉无法达到 85%+ 最大心率。绝不能为节省时间跳过热身。': 'HIIT is high intensity, so the warm-up has to be thorough. Standard flow: (1) 5 minutes of light cardio (jumping jacks, easy jog) to raise body temperature; (2) 3 minutes of dynamic stretching (leg swings, hip rotations, arm circles) to mobilize the joints; (3) 2 minutes of movement-specific activation (slow-motion squats, push-ups, burpees) to rehearse the movement patterns. Ten minutes total. A proper warm-up cuts injury risk by more than 50% and improves HIIT performance — cold muscles simply can\'t reach 85%+ of max heart rate. Never skip the warm-up to save time.',
  'HIIT 热身的标准化流程': 'The Standard HIIT Warm-Up',
  'HIIT 的效果取决于强度。高强度阶段心率须达 80-95% 最大心率，恢复阶段降至 60-70%。心率监控是 HIIT 的必备工具——主观感受（RPE）在 HIIT 中不可靠，因为心理动机会高估强度。建议佩戴心率带或智能手表。如果高强度阶段心率达不到 80%+，说明动作选择或重量不够；如果恢复阶段心率降不到 70% 以下，说明强度过高或休息太短。心率数据让 HIIT 训练从"感觉"变成"科学"。': 'HIIT results depend on intensity. During the work interval, heart rate has to hit 80-95% of max; during recovery it should drop to 60-70%. Heart rate monitoring is essential for HIIT — perceived exertion (RPE) is unreliable here, because motivation makes you overestimate intensity. Wear a heart rate strap or a smartwatch. If your heart rate doesn\'t reach 80%+ during the work interval, your exercise selection or load isn\'t hard enough; if it doesn\'t drop below 70% during recovery, the intensity is too high or the rest too short. Heart rate data turns HIIT from "feel" into science.',
  'HIIT 的核心定义': 'The Core Definition of HIIT',
  'HIIT 的进阶与降阶': 'Progressing and Regressing HIIT',
  'HIIT 的适用人群': 'Who HIIT Is For',
  'HIIT 长期进阶遵循"渐进、轮换、恢复"原则。渐进：每 4 周加 1 个循环或缩短休息 5 秒，避免突然加量。轮换：每 4-8 周切换协议（Tabata→30/30→金字塔）和动作选择，避免适应。恢复：每 8 周安排 1 周"HIIT 减量"（强度降至 70%、循环减半），让身体超量恢复。长期执行 HIIT 者应定期评估关节状态和心率恢复趋势，及时调整。HIIT 不是越强越好，而是 10 年后还能持续训练才是真正的高效。': 'Long-term HIIT progression follows three principles: progress, rotate, recover. Progress: every 4 weeks add one round or cut 5 seconds of rest — never jump the volume suddenly. Rotate: every 4-8 weeks switch protocols (Tabata → 30/30 → pyramid) and exercises to avoid adaptation. Recover: every 8 weeks schedule a "HIIT deload" week (intensity down to 70%, half the rounds) to let the body supercompensate. Anyone doing HIIT long term should regularly assess joint health and heart rate recovery trends and adjust as needed. HIIT isn\'t about going as hard as possible — still being able to train 10 years from now is what makes it effective.',
  'HIIT 需要根据身体状态动态调整。进阶信号：相同协议 RPE 下降、心率恢复加快、动作更流畅——可增加 1 个循环或缩短休息 5 秒。降阶信号：RPE 过高（>9）、心率恢复变慢、动作变形——立即减少循环或延长休息。减脂后期（4-8 周后）身体处于能量不足状态，HIIT 强度可适当降低，避免过度训练。每周评估 RPE 和心率恢复趋势，及时调整。HIIT 不是越累越好，而是越精准越好。': 'HIIT needs to be adjusted dynamically to your physical state. Signs to progress: RPE on the same protocol drops, heart rate recovers faster, movement feels smoother — add a round or cut 5 seconds of rest. Signs to regress: RPE too high (>9), heart rate recovery slowing, form breaking down — immediately cut rounds or extend rest. In the later stages of a cut (after 4-8 weeks) the body is in an energy deficit, so HIIT intensity can be reduced to avoid overtraining. Assess RPE and heart rate recovery trends weekly and adjust in time. HIIT isn\'t about being as exhausted as possible — it\'s about being as precise as possible.',
  'HIIT 频率与恢复': 'HIIT Frequency and Recovery',
  'HIIT高效减脂': 'HIIT for Efficient Fat Loss',
  'HIIT（High-Intensity Interval Training，高强度间歇训练）的核心是"高强度运动 + 主动/被动恢复"的交替循环。高强度阶段心率须达到 80-95% 最大心率（220-年龄），恢复阶段降至 60-70%。一个完整 HIIT 通常 4-8 个循环，总时长 15-25 分钟。与 LISS（低强度稳态有氧）相比，HIIT 时间效率高 3-5 倍、EPOC 效应显著、对肌肉量保留更好，但对关节和神经系统压力更大。': 'The core of HIIT (High-Intensity Interval Training) is alternating cycles of "high-intensity work + active/passive recovery". During the work phase, heart rate has to reach 80-95% of max heart rate (220 - age); during recovery it drops to 60-70%. A full HIIT session is usually 4-8 rounds lasting 15-25 minutes in total. Compared with LISS (low-intensity steady state cardio), HIIT is 3-5 times more time-efficient, produces a significant EPOC effect and preserves muscle mass better, but places more stress on the joints and nervous system.',
  'LP 通常能持续 3-9 个月，当出现以下信号时需要切换到中级方案（如 Texas Method、5/3/1）：①多个主项连续 2 次重启仍无法突破；②单次训练后恢复超过 48 小时；③体重停止增长但训练强度已高。中级方案的核心变化是从"每次训练加重"变为"每周加重"——周一周五训练同一动作但强度不同，给身体更长的适应周期。这是力量训练的进阶逻辑，不是倒退。': 'LP usually lasts 3-9 months. Move on to an intermediate program (such as Texas Method or 5/3/1) when you see these signals: (1) several main lifts stall twice in a row even after a reset; (2) recovery from a single session takes more than 48 hours; (3) body weight stops rising even though intensity is already high. The core change in intermediate programs is moving from "adding weight every session" to "adding weight every week" — you train the same lift on Monday and Friday but at different intensities, giving the body a longer adaptation window. That is the logic of progression in strength training, not a step backwards.',
