  '[GymCardReminder] reschedule: 开关关闭，不调度': '[GymCardReminder] reschedule: toggle is off, not scheduling',
  '[GymCardReminder] reschedule: 无符合条件的卡': '[GymCardReminder] reschedule: no eligible cards',
  '[GymCardReminder] 提醒日 10:00 已过，顺延到 1 分钟后提醒': '[GymCardReminder] Reminder time 10:00 has passed, postponing to 1 minute from now',
  '[GymCardReminder] 精确闹钟不可用，降级为 inexactAllowWhileIdle': '[GymCardReminder] Exact alarm unavailable, falling back to inexactAllowWhileIdle',
  'deload 不是偷懒，而是主动恢复策略。高级训练者长期处于高容量高强度训练中，神经系统、结缔组织、激素水平都会累积疲劳。deload 通过降低容量与强度，让身体超量恢复，消化积累的疲劳。跳过 deload 连续训练 8-12 周后必然出现过度训练，那时被迫休息 2-4 周损失远大于主动 deload 1 周。高级者把 deload 视为训练计划的核心组成部分，不是可选项目。': 'A deload isn\'t slacking — it\'s an active recovery strategy. Advanced trainees spend long stretches at high volume and high intensity, and fatigue accumulates in the nervous system, connective tissue and hormone levels. A deload cuts volume and intensity so the body can supercompensate and digest the accumulated fatigue. Skip deloads and train 8-12 weeks straight, and overtraining is inevitable — the 2-4 weeks of forced rest you\'ll need then costs far more than a planned 1-week deload. Advanced lifters treat the deload as a core part of the program, not an optional extra.',
  'deload 信号：力量退步、睡眠变差、晨起心率上升、握力下降。\n\ndeload 执行：重量降至 70%，组数减半，RPE < 7。\n\n频率：每 4-6 周一次，或出现信号时立即 deload。': 'Deload signals: strength dropping, worse sleep, higher morning heart rate, weaker grip.\n\nHow to deload: drop the weight to 70%, halve the sets, keep RPE under 7.\n\nFrequency: once every 4-6 weeks, or immediately when the signals appear.',
  'deload 减量周': 'Deload Week',
  'deload 周的执行规范': 'How to Run a Deload Week',
  'deload 周的标准执行：重量降至 70% 1RM、组数减半、RPE 控制在 6 以下（保留 4 次以上）、训练频率不变。例如深蹲原 5×5@100kg，deload 周 3×5@70kg。deload 不是完全不练，而是用轻重量维持神经通路和动作模式，同时让身体恢复。完全休息会让积累的训练适应衰减。deload 周不做力竭组、不使用代谢压力技术、不尝试新动作。1 周后回到正常训练时，往往能突破之前的平台。': 'The standard deload week: weight down to 70% of 1RM, half the sets, RPE capped at 6 (4+ reps in reserve), training frequency unchanged. For example, if you normally squat 5×5 at 100 kg, the deload week is 3×5 at 70 kg. A deload isn\'t complete rest — you use light weight to maintain neural pathways and movement patterns while the body recovers. Resting completely lets accumulated training adaptations decay. No failure sets during a deload week, no metabolic stress techniques, no new exercises. When you return to normal training a week later, you\'ll often break through the plateau you were stuck on.',
  'deload 有两种安排方式：①定期 deload——每 4-6 周固定安排 1 周，可预测、易执行；②自调节 deload——根据 RPE 和身体信号灵活安排，更精准但需要经验。高级者推荐自调节 deload，结合训练日志的 RPE 趋势和晨起心率监测。当连续 2 周主项 RPE 上升 1 分以上、或晨起心率连续 3 天上升 5 次以上，立即 deload。这种自调节方式比固定周期更高效，避免"按计划该 deload 但状态正好"的浪费。': 'There are two ways to schedule deloads: (1) fixed deload — one week every 4-6 weeks, predictable and easy to follow; (2) autoregulated deload — scheduled flexibly based on RPE and physical signals, more precise but requires experience. Advanced lifters are better off with autoregulated deloads, combining RPE trends from their training log with morning heart rate monitoring. Deload immediately when your main lift RPE rises by more than 1 point for two weeks in a row, or when morning heart rate rises by more than 5 beats for three straight days. This autoregulated approach is more efficient than a fixed cycle and avoids the waste of "it\'s time to deload on paper but I\'m feeling great".',
  'deload 的周期化安排': 'Programming Deloads',
  'deload 的本质与必要性': 'Why Deloads Matter',
  'drop set 是最有效的代谢压力技术。执行：选择 10RM 重量做到力竭（约 10 次），立即降重量 30% 继续做到力竭（约 8 次），再降 30% 做到力竭（约 6 次），完成一次 drop set。每个动作只做 1-2 次 drop set，放在训练最末段。drop set 的代谢压力极强，每个肌群每周不超过 2 次。研究显示，drop set 在肌肥大效果上与 3 组标准组相当，但时间缩短 50%，适合高级者突破平台。': 'The drop set is the most effective metabolic stress technique. How to do it: pick a 10RM load and go to failure (about 10 reps), immediately drop the weight by 30% and continue to failure (about 8 reps), then drop another 30% and go to failure (about 6 reps) — that completes one drop set. Do only 1-2 drop sets per exercise, at the very end of the session. Drop sets create enormous metabolic stress, so cap them at 2 per muscle group per week. Research shows drop sets produce hypertrophy comparable to 3 standard sets in half the time, making them a good plateau-breaker for advanced lifters.',
  'drop set 的执行细节': 'Drop Set Execution Details',
