  '不同意并退出': 'Disagree and exit',
  '不同目标（增肌/减脂/塑形/健康）对应不同器械策略。本章教你快速制定自己的器械路线图，并掌握安全使用铁律。': 'Different goals (muscle gain / fat loss / shaping / health) call for different equipment strategies. This chapter shows you how to quickly build your own equipment roadmap and master the non-negotiable safety rules.',
  '不憋气': 'Don\'t hold your breath',
  '不收集个人信息': 'We don\'t collect personal information',
  '不收集姓名、手机号、通讯录等个人敏感信息': 'We don\'t collect names, phone numbers, contacts or other sensitive personal information',
  '不是吃得更少，而是吃得更准。减脂不是饥饿游戏，而是用科学方法让身体在热量缺口中稳定燃烧脂肪。记录和计算是减脂期的两只眼睛——前者告诉你正在吃什么，后者告诉你应该吃什么。': 'It\'s not about eating less, it\'s about eating smarter. Fat loss isn\'t a hunger game — it\'s about using a scientific approach to keep your body burning fat steadily in a calorie deficit. Tracking and calculating are your two eyes during a cut: the first tells you what you\'re eating, the second tells you what you should be eating.',
  '不甩动借力': 'Don\'t swing for momentum',
  '不管什么饮食法——低碳、低脂、间歇禁食、生酮——减脂的本质都是热量消耗大于摄入。理解这一点，你就不会被各种花哨的饮食概念迷惑，也不会被某些所谓的神奇减脂食物误导。缺口大小决定减脂速度，但过大的缺口会带来肌肉流失、代谢下降、内分泌紊乱，最终引发暴食反弹。减脂不是越快越好，而是越可持续越好。': 'Whatever the diet — low carb, low fat, intermittent fasting, keto — fat loss always comes down to burning more calories than you take in. Once you understand that, no flashy diet concept will fool you and no so-called magic fat-burning food will mislead you. The size of the deficit determines how fast you lose fat, but too large a deficit brings muscle loss, a slower metabolism and hormonal disruption, and ends in a binge rebound. Fat loss isn\'t about being as fast as possible — it\'s about being as sustainable as possible.',
  '不耸肩不借力': 'Don\'t shrug, don\'t use momentum',
  '不能输入自己的邀请码': 'You can\'t enter your own invite code',
  '不能输入自己的邀请码哦': 'You can\'t enter your own invite code',
  '不自由落体': 'No free-falling',
  '不要盲目继续削减热量至极低水平（低于 BMR），会导致暴食反弹、代谢进一步下降、内分泌紊乱': 'Don\'t blindly keep cutting calories to an extremely low level (below BMR); it leads to a binge rebound, further metabolic slowdown and hormonal disruption',
  '不要追求"完美饮食"。80% 时间健康饮食 + 20% 灵活食物，是长期坚持的关键。极端饮食必然导致暴食反弹': 'Don\'t chase a "perfect diet". Eating healthy 80% of the time plus 20% flexible foods is the key to long-term consistency. Extreme dieting inevitably leads to a binge rebound',
  '不超肩关节活动度': 'Stay within shoulder range of motion',
  '不锁死膝关节': 'Don\'t lock out the knees',
  '不错嘛，再来一局？': 'Not bad — another round?',
  '不需要任何器械，只靠自身体重就能完成全身训练。本章介绍 8 个居家核心动作，覆盖下肢、上肢、核心，帮你随时随地完成系统训练。': 'No equipment needed — bodyweight alone is enough for a full-body workout. This chapter introduces 8 core home exercises covering the lower body, upper body and core, so you can train systematically anytime, anywhere.',
  '不需要健身房，只要一对哑铃和一块垫子，就能练遍全身。4 章含 8 大动作图解：分清每个动作练哪里、怎么做、多少组。居家新手照着练，一套全身哑铃计划轻松拿下。': 'No gym required — a pair of dumbbells and a mat is all you need to train your whole body. 4 chapters with illustrated guides to 8 key exercises: what each one works, how to do it, and how many sets. Home beginners can follow along and nail a full-body dumbbell routine.',
  '与对手打平！再来一次拉开差距': 'Tied with your opponent! Go again to break the tie',
  '专属称号': 'Exclusive Title',
  '专题': 'Topic',
  '专题教学包': 'Themed Tutorial Pack',
  '丢弃': 'Discard',
  '个人中心': 'Profile',
  '个人信息已更新': 'Profile updated',
  '个人记录': 'Personal Records',
  '个体化是高级训练的核心。需要考虑的关键变量：①基因差异——同样的训练，基因优势者恢复更快、增长更多，不能盲目照搬他人方案；②恢复能力——睡眠 8 小时 vs 6 小时的训练者，可承受容量差 30%；③训练经验——3 年 vs 5 年的训练者，对相同容量的响应不同；④生活方式——高压工作 vs 自由职业者，可承受训练频率不同。这些变量决定最优方案，需要通过日志和实验找到自己的"甜点"。': 'Individualization is the core of advanced training. Key variables to consider: ① genetic differences — with the same program, genetically gifted trainees recover faster and gain more, so never copy someone else\'s plan blindly; ② recovery capacity — someone sleeping 8 hours vs 6 hours can handle about 30% more volume; ③ training experience — 3 years vs 5 years of training produces different responses to the same volume; ④ lifestyle — a high-stress job vs freelancing means a different tolerable training frequency. These variables determine your optimal plan, and you have to find your own "sweet spot" through logging and experimentation.',
  '个体化的关键变量': 'Key variables of individualization',
  '个性化训练计划': 'Personalized training plan',
  '中午': 'Noon',
  '中周期与长期规划': 'Mesocycles and long-term planning',
  '中段补水': 'Hydrate mid-session',
  '中等强度：150-300 分钟/周，心率 60-70% 最大心率\n高强度：75-150 分钟/周，心率 70-85% 最大心率\n最大心率估算：220 - 年龄（如 30 岁 = 190）\n频率：每周 3-5 次，每次 30-45 分钟\n组合：中等+高强度混合效果最佳': 'Moderate intensity: 150-300 minutes/week at 60-70% of max heart rate\nHigh intensity: 75-150 minutes/week at 70-85% of max heart rate\nMax heart rate estimate: 220 - age (e.g. age 30 = 190)\nFrequency: 3-5 times a week, 30-45 minutes per session\nCombination: mixing moderate and high intensity works best',
  '中级': 'Intermediate',
  '中级塑形进阶': 'Intermediate shaping progression',
  '中级训练者仍固守线性进阶（5×5）无法突破平台，应切换至周期化（5/3/1/Texas Method）': 'Intermediate trainees still stuck on linear progression (5×5) won\'t break through plateaus; switch to periodization (5/3/1 / Texas Method)',
  '中老年人在开始新运动计划前，应先进行科学的自我健康评估。本章介绍健康自评清单、运动禁忌与安全原则，让你在安全的前提下开始健身。': 'Before starting a new exercise program, middle-aged and older adults should do a proper self-assessment of their health. This chapter covers a health self-check list, exercise contraindications and safety principles, so you can start training safely.',
  '中老年人的身体机能在自然退化，开始运动前进行健康评估至关重要。如果你患有高血压、心脏病、糖尿病、关节病等慢性疾病，或一段时间内有过胸闷、气短、头晕等症状，都应先咨询医生再开始运动。量力而行不是退缩，而是对自己身体最大的负责。': 'Physical function naturally declines with age, so a health check before starting exercise is essential. If you have chronic conditions such as high blood pressure, heart disease, diabetes or joint problems, or you\'ve had chest tightness, shortness of breath or dizziness recently, consult a doctor before starting. Knowing your limits isn\'t backing down — it\'s the greatest responsibility you can take for your body.',
  '中老年科学健身': 'Science-Based Fitness for Older Adults',
  '中老年运动不必依赖心率表，一个简单的"说话测试"足以把握强度：运动中能轻松交谈但微喘——中等强度，最理想；勉强能挤出几个字——偏强，应放慢；能顺畅唱歌——强度过低。每天保证 30 分钟中等强度活动，就是良好的健康投资。': 'Older adults don\'t need a heart rate monitor to gauge intensity — a simple "talk test" is enough: if you can talk comfortably but are slightly breathless during exercise, that\'s moderate intensity and ideal; if you can barely squeeze out a few words, it\'s too hard and you should slow down; if you can sing smoothly, the intensity is too low. Getting 30 minutes of moderate activity a day is a solid investment in your health.',
