  '今日风速宜训': 'Wind\'s up, a good day to train',
  '从 30 岁起肌肉量以每十年 3-8% 的速度流失，这就是"肌少症"。缺乏肌肉会导致行动迟缓、易疲劳、代谢下降，甚至增加跌倒和骨折风险。规律的力量训练能有效延缓肌肉流失，提升基础代谢与生活质量。力量不是年轻人的专利，而是中老年人最值得的投资。': 'From age 30, muscle mass is lost at 3-8% per decade — that\'s "sarcopenia". Too little muscle leads to slower movement, easy fatigue and a lower metabolism, and even raises the risk of falls and fractures. Regular strength training slows muscle loss effectively and raises your basal metabolism and quality of life. Strength isn\'t a young person\'s privilege — it\'s the best investment an older adult can make.',
  '从 LP 到中级阶段': 'From LP to the intermediate stage',
  '从入门到精通的完整训练体系': 'A complete training system from beginner to advanced',
  '从分享到双方获奖的完整链路': 'The full path from sharing to rewards for both sides',
  '从剪贴板粘贴': 'Paste from clipboard',
  '从剪贴板粘贴数据': 'Paste data from clipboard',
  '从器材使用到饮食计划，5章完整闭环': 'From equipment use to meal planning, 5 chapters forming a complete loop',
  '从快走过渡到慢跑，速度以能正常对话为宜（约60-70%最大心率），身体微前倾，目视前方。': 'Ease from a brisk walk into a jog at a pace where you can still hold a conversation (about 60-70% of max heart rate), lean the body slightly forward and look straight ahead.',
  '从慢走过渡到慢跑，坡度保持5-8%，步伐缩小，前脚掌着地，臀部发力蹬地推进。': 'Transition from a slow walk to a jog, keep the incline at 5-8%, shorten your stride, land on the forefoot and push through the glutes.',
  '从热量缺口到宏量营养素分配，从食材选择到平台期突破，系统化掌握减脂期饮食管理的所有关键点。': 'From calorie deficit to macronutrient split, from food choices to breaking plateaus — systematically master every key point of diet management during a cut.',
  '从相册选择': 'Choose from album',
  '从相册选择二维码图片': 'Choose a QR code image from gallery',
  '从零基础到进阶的完整体系': 'A complete system from beginner to advanced',
  '从零开始也能轻松上手，快来看看怎么创建吧': 'Easy to start even from zero — come see how to create one',
  '从顶端位置控制身体缓慢下放至完全伸展，背阔肌充分拉伸，下放过程2-3秒，保持张力不松手。': 'From the top position, lower yourself slowly under control to full extension, letting the lats stretch fully; the lowering phase takes 2-3 seconds, keeping tension without letting go.',
  '代谢压力技术放在训练末段使用，每周 1-2 次。在主项前使用会损害力量表现，影响机械张力刺激': 'Use metabolic stress techniques at the end of a session, 1-2 times a week. Using them before your main lifts hurts strength output and blunts the mechanical tension stimulus',
  '代谢压力技术最适合孤立动作和辅助动作，不适合大重量复合动作。例如：训练末段的二头弯举用 drop set、侧平举用三联组、腿屈伸用 21 响。每周 1-2 次训练应用，其余训练保持标准组。每个肌群每周接受 1 次代谢压力训练即可，过多会干扰恢复。在减量周完全不使用代谢压力技术，让身体充分恢复。': 'Metabolic stress techniques work best for isolation and accessory movements, not heavy compounds. For example: drop sets on bicep curls at the end of a session, tri-sets on lateral raises, 21s on leg extensions. Apply them in 1-2 sessions a week and keep the rest of your sessions as straight sets. One metabolic stress session per muscle group per week is enough — more interferes with recovery. Skip them entirely during deload weeks so your body can fully recover.',
  '代谢压力机制：TUT 延长 + 组间短休息 + 高次数。\n\n技术：超级组/三联组/drop set/21响/部分幅度。\n\n应用：放在训练末段，每周 1-2 次，避免滥用。': 'Metabolic stress mechanism: extended TUT + short rest between sets + high reps.\n\nTechniques: supersets / tri-sets / drop sets / 21s / partial range.\n\nApplication: use at the end of a session, 1-2 times a week, avoid overuse.',
  '代谢压力的肌肥大机制': 'The hypertrophy mechanism of metabolic stress',
  '以上字段均为可选，可直接点击"下一步"跳过': 'All fields above are optional; you can tap "Next" to skip',
  '以低于目标配速1分钟的速度起步2-3公里，逐步进入匀速区间，避免起跑过快导致后程掉速。': 'Start 2-3 km at a pace one minute slower than your target pace, then ease into your steady-state zone to avoid going out too fast and fading later.',
  '以接近全力（85-95%最大心率）冲刺跑30-60秒，摆臂有力，前脚掌着地，保持正确跑姿。': 'Sprint at close to full effort (85-95% of max heart rate) for 30-60 seconds, driving the arms hard, landing on the forefoot and holding good running form.',
  '以身作则，今日开训': 'Lead by example — start training today',
  '仰卧举腿': 'Lying Leg Raise',
  '仰卧于卧推凳，双眼位于杠铃正下方': 'Lie on the bench with your eyes directly under the barbell',
  '仰卧于卧推凳，双脚踩实地面、肩胛骨后缩下沉形成"起桥"。握距略宽于肩，全握杠铃（拇指环绕）。下放时肘部约 45° 外展、触胸位置在乳头至胸骨下端之间。推起时双脚蹬地传力、杠铃轨迹垂直向上。卧推的关键是肩胛稳定——后缩下沉的肩胛是力量传递的基础，松动的肩胛会让推力泄漏到凳面。': 'Lie on the bench with your feet planted firmly on the floor and your shoulder blades retracted and depressed to form an "arch". Grip slightly wider than shoulder width with a full grip (thumb wrapped). On the way down, flare the elbows about 45° and touch the bar between the nipples and the bottom of the sternum. As you press, drive through your feet and keep the bar path vertical. The key to the bench press is scapular stability — retracted and depressed shoulder blades are the foundation of force transfer, and loose shoulder blades leak your push into the bench.',
  '仰卧于垫上，双腿屈膝约90度，双脚掌着地（或抬腿），双手轻放耳侧，下背部贴紧地面。': 'Lie on the mat with the knees bent about 90 degrees and the soles of your feet on the floor (or legs raised), hands resting lightly beside the ears, lower back pressed into the floor.',
  '仰卧于平凳上，双脚踩实地面，肩胛骨后缩下沉贴凳。双手持哑铃于胸部正上方伸直，掌心相对，肘关节微屈约20-30度并固定角度。': 'Lie on a flat bench with your feet planted firmly, shoulder blades retracted and depressed into the bench. Hold the dumbbells straight up over the chest with palms facing each other, elbows slightly bent about 20-30 degrees and locked at that angle.',
  '仰卧于平凳上，双脚踩实地面，肩胛骨后缩下沉，挺胸收腹。双手正握杠铃，握距略宽于肩，腕关节保持中立位，肘关节微屈。': 'Lie on a flat bench with your feet planted firmly, shoulder blades retracted and depressed, chest up and core braced. Grip the barbell with an overhand grip slightly wider than shoulder width, wrists neutral and elbows slightly bent.',
  '仰卧凳上，双手持哑铃于胸口上方': 'Lie on the bench holding the dumbbells above your chest',
  '仰卧凳上，手臂垂直于胸口': 'Lie on the bench with your arms perpendicular to your chest',
  '仰卧双手置于臀部下方': 'Lie on your back with your hands under your glutes',
  '仰卧屈膝，双手轻扶头侧': 'Lie on your back with knees bent, hands lightly supporting the head',
  '仰卧臂屈伸': 'Lying Triceps Extension',
