  '休闲': 'Casual',
  '优势：单次容量最大可专项强化薄弱肌群，配合FST-7（7组×10-12次组间拉伸30秒）作为收尾': 'Advantage: the largest per-session volume lets you specialize on weak muscle groups, finishing with FST-7 (7 sets × 10-12 reps with 30 seconds of stretching between sets)',
  '优势：每肌群48-72小时恢复窗口，训练频率高，符合频率meta分析每周2次优于1次的肌肥大结论': 'Advantage: a 48-72 hour recovery window per muscle group with high training frequency, matching the frequency meta-analysis showing 2 sessions per week beats 1 for hypertrophy',
  '优势：每肌群获得充分训练容量同时保留48-72小时恢复，避免高频率下的累积疲劳': 'Advantage: each muscle group gets enough training volume while still keeping 48-72 hours of recovery, avoiding accumulated fatigue from high frequency',
  '优势：训练频率与容量最大化，可针对每个肌群进行深度精雕，适合备赛或极限突破': 'Advantage: training frequency and volume are maximized, allowing detailed work on every muscle group — ideal for contest prep or breaking through limits',
  '优质碳水清单': 'Quality Carb List',
  '优质脂肪清单': 'Healthy Fat List',
  '优质蛋白清单': 'Quality Protein List',
  '优质蛋白：鸡胸肉、鱼虾、蛋白、瘦牛肉、希腊酸奶。\n\n优质碳水：燕麦、糙米、红薯、全麦面包。\n\n优质脂肪：牛油果、坚果、橄榄油、鱼油。\n\n避坑食物：含糖饮料、深加工食品、油炸食品、精制碳水。\n\n外食技巧：选烤/蒸/煮而非炸，酱料分开蘸，先吃菜再吃肉最后吃主食。': 'Quality protein: chicken breast, fish and shrimp, egg whites, lean beef, Greek yogurt.\n\nQuality carbs: oats, brown rice, sweet potato, whole wheat bread.\n\nHealthy fats: avocado, nuts, olive oil, fish oil.\n\nFoods to avoid: sugary drinks, heavily processed foods, fried foods, refined carbs.\n\nEating out tips: choose grilled/steamed/boiled instead of fried, get sauce on the side, and eat vegetables first, then protein, then carbs.',
  '优雅': 'Graceful',
  '传承不息': 'The legacy lives on',
  '传承导师': 'Legacy Mentor',
  '传承裁决': 'Legacy Verdict',
  '传统硬拉起始：杠铃贴近胫骨中段、双脚与髋同宽、握距略宽于小腿。髋部铰链前倾、膝盖微屈、背部保持中立。起把时先腿后背——膝盖先伸、然后髋部前推、最后挺胸收肩。全程杠铃贴近身体，离地后沿小腿、膝盖、大腿滑动至髋部。硬拉的关键是杠铃路径——任何远离身体的偏移都会成倍增加腰部负荷和受伤风险。': 'Conventional deadlift setup: bar close to mid-shin, feet hip-width apart, grip just outside the shins. Hinge at the hips, bend the knees slightly and keep the back neutral. On the pull, legs first then back — the knees extend, then the hips drive forward, and finally you lift the chest and set the shoulders. Keep the bar close to the body throughout, sliding along the shins, knees and thighs up to the hips. The key to the deadlift is bar path — any drift away from the body multiplies the load on your lower back and the risk of injury.',
  '估算': 'Estimate',
  '伸肘回到起始位置': 'Extend the elbows back to the starting position',
  '低于目标配速起步': 'Start slower than target pace',
  '低冲击有氧形式对比': 'Comparison of low-impact cardio options',
  '低头或仰头': 'Head dropped or tilted back',
  '低强度恢复': 'Low-intensity recovery',
  '低杠位（躯干前倾）髋矩大、膝矩小，适合髋强；高杠位反之，应根据个体强项选择': 'A low bar position (more forward lean) means a larger hip moment and a smaller knee moment, suiting hip-dominant lifters; a high bar position is the opposite — choose according to your own strengths',
  '体系切换时机：LP连续3次失败→5/3/1或Texas Method；GZCLP失败后重启T1测新5RM取85%重新爬升': 'When to switch systems: 3 consecutive LP failures → 5/3/1 or Texas Method; after a GZCLP failure, restart T1 by testing a new 5RM and working back up from 85%',
  '体脂率': 'Body Fat Percentage',
  '体脂率 (%)': 'Body Fat (%)',
  '体脂率过高时过度训练腹肌，腹肌被脂肪覆盖无法显现，应优先热量赤字降体脂': 'Overtraining abs when body fat is too high won\'t show — the abs are covered by fat, so prioritize a calorie deficit to lower body fat first',
  '体重': 'Weight',
  '体重 (kg)': 'Weight (kg)',
  '体重下降后基础代谢随之降低——每减 1kg 体重约减少 15-20 大卡 TDEE，10kg 就是 150-200 大卡。同时身体会进入节能模式主动降低 NEAT（非运动消耗），你下意识少动、少抖腿、少走动。再加上水分波动和热量计算误差（多数人会低估 20-30%），平台期是减脂的必然阶段，遇到它不意味着失败，而是身体在适应新体重。': 'As weight drops, your basal metabolism drops with it — every 1kg lost cuts TDEE by roughly 15-20 calories, so 10kg means 150-200 calories. At the same time your body switches into energy-saving mode and actively reduces NEAT (non-exercise activity thermogenesis): you subconsciously move less, fidget less and walk less. Add in water retention and calorie tracking errors (most people underestimate by 20-30%), and a plateau becomes an inevitable stage of fat loss. Hitting one doesn\'t mean you failed — it means your body is adapting to your new weight.',
  '体重保持稳定，继续坚持！': 'Weight is holding steady — keep going!',
