  '保持正常呼吸，不憋气': 'Breathe normally, don\'t hold your breath',
  '保持稳定': 'Stay stable',
  '保持稳定的中等配速，呼吸节奏三步一吸两步一呼，核心稳定，步频170-180步/分钟。': 'Hold a steady moderate pace with a three-steps-in, two-steps-out breathing rhythm, core stable and cadence at 170-180 steps per minute.',
  '保持稳定，继续努力': 'Stay consistent, keep pushing',
  '保持肘关节固定角度，沿弧线缓慢向两侧打开哑铃，感受胸大肌拉伸，下放至与肩同高或略低，下放过程吸气。': 'Keep the elbow angle fixed and open the dumbbells slowly out to the sides along an arc, feeling the stretch in the pecs; lower to shoulder height or slightly below and inhale on the way down.',
  '保持肩胛骨下沉稳定': 'Keep the shoulder blades depressed and stable',
  '保持脊柱中立位，挺胸': 'Keep the spine neutral and the chest up',
  '保持自然呼吸，发力时呼气，还原时吸气': 'Breathe naturally: exhale on exertion, inhale on the way back',
  '保持自然腹式呼吸，吸气时腹部扩张，呼气时腹部收紧，避免憋气导致血压升高，维持稳定。': 'Breathe naturally with diaphragmatic breathing — the belly expands as you inhale and tightens as you exhale — avoid holding your breath and raising blood pressure, and stay stable.',
  '保持节奏': 'Keep the rhythm',
  '保证后台计时和提醒正常工作': 'Keep background timing and reminders working properly',
  '修改成功': 'Updated successfully',
  '俯卧于垫上，双肘弯曲支撑于肩部正下方，前臂平行贴地，双脚并拢脚尖撑地，身体呈一条直线准备。': 'Lie face down on the mat with the elbows bent and planted directly under the shoulders, forearms parallel on the floor, feet together and toes on the ground, body in a straight line and ready.',
  '俯卧撑': 'Push-up',
  '俯卧撑起始姿势': 'Push-up starting position',
  '俯身哑铃划船：俯身屈髋，双手持铃沿大腿向髋部拉 — 主练背部': 'Bent-over dumbbell row: hinge at the hips and pull the dumbbells along the thighs toward the hips — mainly works the back',
  '借力摆动': 'Swinging for Momentum',
  '借力摆动身体': 'Swinging the Body for Momentum',
  '借力甩动身体靠惯性完成弯举，肘部前后移动使二头失去稳定发力': 'Swinging the body to curl the weight with momentum, with the elbows drifting forward and back so the biceps lose stable tension',
  '倾斜角过大（>45°）变成肩推': 'Too much incline (>45°) turns it into a shoulder press',
  '偏瘦': 'Underweight',
  '偏胖': 'Overweight',
  '停顿1秒感受收缩': 'Pause 1 second to feel the contraction',
  '健将': 'Athlete',
  '健康': 'Health',
  '健康保持指南': 'Health Maintenance Guide',
  '健康导向训练不以最大力量、最大围度、最低体脂为目标，而以"30 年后还能否独立完成日常活动"为终点。研究显示，30 岁后每十年流失 3-8% 肌肉量，60 岁后加速；力量训练能将流失率降至 1-2%。心肺功能、骨密度、关节灵活度同样遵循"用进废退"。健康训练的目标是建立可持续 30 年的训练习惯，而非短期突破。': 'Health-oriented training doesn\'t aim for maximum strength, maximum size or lowest body fat — the goal is "can you still handle daily activities independently 30 years from now". Research shows muscle mass drops 3-8% per decade after 30 and the loss accelerates after 60; strength training can cut that rate to 1-2%. Cardio capacity, bone density and joint mobility follow the same "use it or lose it" rule. The goal of training for health is to build a habit you can sustain for 30 years, not a short-term breakthrough.',
  '健康期营养不以增肌或减脂为目标，而以"维持稳定的身体成分和代谢健康"为核心。蛋白质 1.2-1.6g/kg 足够保留肌肉量；碳水占总热量 45-55% 提供训练能量；脂肪占 25-30% 维持激素水平。关键是避免极端饮食——生酮、断食、极低热量在短期内可能有效，但长期执行率低、代谢副作用大。均衡饮食 + 适量热量是 30 年可持续的方案。': 'Nutrition for a health phase doesn\'t aim to build muscle or lose fat — its core is "maintaining stable body composition and metabolic health". Protein at 1.2-1.6g/kg is enough to preserve muscle; carbs at 45-55% of total calories fuel training; fat at 25-30% supports hormone levels. The key is avoiding extreme diets — keto, fasting and very low calorie can work short term, but long-term adherence is poor and the metabolic side effects are real. A balanced diet with adequate calories is the plan you can sustain for 30 years.',
  '健康期营养的核心理念': 'Core principles of nutrition for a health phase',
  '健康训练 30 年的关键不是单次训练多努力，而是能否持续。三个策略：①习惯化——固定训练时间（如每周一三五早晨），降低决策成本；②社交化——找训练伙伴或加入社群，社交压力成为坚持动力；③目标化——设置非体型目标（如深蹲 1.5 倍体重、5 公里跑 25 分钟、连续训练 100 周），让训练有可衡量的进步。健康是马拉松，节奏比冲刺重要。': 'The key to 30 years of training for health isn\'t how hard any single session is, it\'s whether you can keep going. Three strategies: ① make it a habit — fix your training times (e.g. Monday, Wednesday and Friday mornings) to cut decision costs; ② make it social — find a training partner or join a community so social pressure fuels consistency; ③ set goals — use non-appearance goals (squat 1.5× bodyweight, run 5 km in 25 minutes, train 100 weeks straight) so progress is measurable. Health is a marathon; pace matters more than sprinting.',
  '健康训练 ≠ 健美训练：强度适中、频率稳定、关节友好。\n\n四大支柱：力量保留 / 心肺功能 / 关节灵活 / 生活方式。\n\n年龄考量：30+ 岁恢复能力下降，需更多恢复与多样性。': 'Training for health ≠ bodybuilding training: moderate intensity, steady frequency, joint friendly.\n\nFour pillars: strength retention / cardio capacity / joint mobility / lifestyle.\n\nAge considerations: recovery capacity declines after 30+, so you need more recovery and more variety.',
  '健康训练优先低冲击有氧。跑步对膝盖冲击是体重的 2-3 倍，骑行和椭圆机只有 0.5 倍，长期执行更安全': 'Training for health prioritizes low-impact cardio. Running hits the knees with 2-3 times body weight, while cycling and the elliptical are only 0.5 times — safer for the long run',
  '健康训练的优先级': 'Priorities of training for health',
  '健康训练的优先级是：恢复 > 营养 > 心肺 > 力量 > 灵活。许多人倒置顺序，先练力量再管睡眠，结果长期处于过度训练边缘。正确做法是先保证睡眠 7 小时、蛋白质 1.2g/kg、每周 150 分钟有氧，再叠加 2 次力量训练。这样的顺序让身体始终处于"能恢复"的状态，训练才能持续 30 年。健康训练不是练得多，而是练得对。': 'The priority order for training health is: recovery > nutrition > cardio > strength > mobility. Many people flip it, training strength first and dealing with sleep later, leaving them permanently on the edge of overtraining. The right approach is to lock in 7 hours of sleep, 1.2g/kg of protein and 150 minutes of cardio per week first, then add 2 strength sessions on top. That order keeps your body in a state where it can recover, so training can last 30 years. Training for health isn\'t about training more — it\'s about training right.',
  '健康训练的差异化定位': 'What sets training for health apart',
  '健康训练的核心是"可持续"。一次高强度训练不如十次中等强度训练，关键是 10 年后仍在训练': 'The core of training for health is "sustainability". One high-intensity session is worth less than ten moderate ones — what matters is still training 10 years from now',
  '健康训练负荷取 60-75% 1RM，2-3 组×10-12 次，保留 2-3 RIR 避免力竭。这种安排在保留肌肉量的同时不给关节和神经系统过度压力。重量选择以"做完 12 次还能再做 2-3 次"为准。每周 2 次全身训练，覆盖胸/背/腿/肩/核心 5 大肌群，每次 6-8 个动作，总训练时长 45-60 分钟。这种容量足以保留肌肉量，又不影响恢复。': 'For health, load 60-75% of 1RM for 2-3 sets × 10-12 reps, keeping 2-3 RIR and avoiding failure. This preserves muscle without overloading the joints and nervous system. Pick a weight where you could still do 2-3 more reps after 12. Train the whole body twice a week, covering the 5 major muscle groups — chest / back / legs / shoulders / core — with 6-8 exercises per session for 45-60 minutes total. That\'s enough volume to maintain muscle without hurting recovery.',
