  '周期': 'Cycle',
  '周期化安排：每4周为一个微周期，第4周减量50%进行主动恢复': 'Periodization: each 4 weeks is one microcycle, with a 50% volume reduction in week 4 for active recovery',
  '周期化（5/3/1）：4周一循环（5/3/1+deload），FSL 5×5或BBB 5×10辅助，每周期TM+2.5-5kg，适合中级': 'Periodization (5/3/1): a 4-week cycle (5/3/1 + deload), FSL 5×5 or BBB 5×10 assistance, TM +2.5-5kg per cycle, suitable for intermediates',
  '周末战士·平时加班的运营': 'Weekend warrior · an operations specialist who works late on weekdays',
  '呼吸与发力节奏': 'Breathing and Force Tempo',
  '呼吸与变式': 'Breathing and Variations',
  '呼吸加压：动作前深吸气到腹部，憋气完成一次重复，吐气在顶部\n脊柱中立：保持自然生理曲度，不龟背不过度反弓\n控制离心：离心阶段 2-3 秒，不靠重力自由落体\n核心稳定：腹肌+腰肌同步收紧，维持腹内压\n鞋具选择：硬底平底鞋或举重鞋，不穿跑步鞋': 'Bracing breath: take a deep breath into the belly before the rep, hold it through the rep, exhale at the top\nNeutral spine: maintain natural curves — no rounding, no excessive arching\nControlled eccentric: 2-3 seconds on the lowering phase, don\'t let gravity drop the weight\nCore stability: brace the abs and lower back together to maintain intra-abdominal pressure\nFootwear: hard, flat-soled shoes or lifting shoes — no running shoes',
  '呼吸节奏': 'Breathing Rhythm',
  '呼吸节奏均匀': 'Even breathing rhythm',
  '呼吸节奏稳定': 'Steady breathing rhythm',
  '哑铃': 'Dumbbell',
  '哑铃/器械': 'Dumbbell/Machine',
  '哑铃/杠铃': 'Dumbbell/Barbell',
  '哑铃/自重': 'Dumbbell/Bodyweight',
  '哑铃/药球': 'Dumbbell/Medicine Ball',
  '哑铃下放至与肩同高，胸大肌充分拉伸，停顿1秒感受拉伸感，不追求过大活动度以免肩关节受伤，保持肩胛贴凳。': 'Lower the dumbbells to shoulder height for a full stretch of the pecs, pause 1 second to feel the stretch, don\'t chase excessive range of motion that could injure the shoulder, and keep the shoulder blades on the bench.',
  '哑铃举至与肩同高（肘部与肩平齐），停顿1秒感受中束收缩，不高于肩避免斜方肌过度代偿。': 'Raise the dumbbells to shoulder height (elbows level with the shoulders), pause 1 second to feel the medial delt contract, and don\'t go above shoulder height to avoid excessive trap compensation.',
  '哑铃位于肩部两侧，掌心朝前，肘关节约呈90度，腕关节中立，核心收紧不塌腰，准备三角肌发力。': 'Dumbbells at the sides of the shoulders, palms facing forward, elbows at about 90 degrees, wrists neutral, core braced without arching the lower back, ready to drive with the delts.',
  '哑铃侧平举': 'Dumbbell Lateral Raise',
  '哑铃俄罗斯转体：坐姿持铃，左右交替转动躯干 — 主练腹部': 'Dumbbell Russian Twist: seated holding a dumbbell, rotate the torso side to side — primarily targets the abs',
  '哑铃卧推：仰卧垫上，双手持铃推起至胸上方 — 主练胸大肌': 'Dumbbell Bench Press: lying on a mat, press the dumbbells up over the chest — primarily targets the pecs',
  '哑铃回到胸部正上方，掌心相对，肘关节保持微屈，肩胛稳定贴凳，完成一次重复，注意哑铃不互相碰撞。': 'Return the dumbbells directly over the chest, palms facing each other, elbows slightly bent, shoulder blades stable on the bench to complete one rep; make sure the dumbbells don\'t knock into each other.',
  '哑铃弯举': 'Dumbbell Curl',
  '哑铃弯举是肱二头肌的经典训练动作，简单有效。': 'The dumbbell curl is a classic biceps exercise — simple and effective.',
  '哑铃弯举至肩部，肱二头肌顶峰收缩1秒，肘部保持贴身，不耸肩，小指可微外旋强化收缩。': 'Curl the dumbbell up to shoulder level, hold the peak biceps contraction for 1 second, keep the elbows tucked in, don\'t shrug, and slightly rotate the pinky outward to strengthen the contraction.',
  '哑铃弯举至肩部，肱桡肌顶峰收缩1秒，掌心保持相对，肘部贴身不前移，不耸肩借力。': 'Curl the dumbbell to shoulder level, hold the peak brachioradialis contraction for 1 second, keep the palms facing each other, elbows tucked without drifting forward, and don\'t shrug to cheat.',
  '哑铃弯举：手臂自然下垂，屈肘将铃举起 — 主练肱二头肌': 'Dumbbell Curl: arms hanging naturally, bend the elbow to curl the weight up — primarily targets the biceps',
  '哑铃推举': 'Dumbbell Shoulder Press',
  '哑铃推举主要锻炼三角肌中束和前束，是肩部训练的核心动作。': 'The dumbbell press mainly works the medial and anterior deltoids and is a core shoulder exercise.',
  '哑铃深蹲：双手持铃于胸前，下蹲臀部低于膝盖 — 主练臀腿': 'Dumbbell Squat: hold dumbbells at the chest, squat until the hips drop below the knees — primarily targets glutes and legs',
  '哑铃箭步蹲：向前迈步下蹲，前后膝各呈 90 度 — 主练臀腿': 'Dumbbell Lunge: step forward and squat down so both knees reach 90 degrees — primarily targets glutes and legs',
  '哑铃罗马尼亚硬拉': 'Dumbbell Romanian Deadlift',
  '哑铃肩上推举：坐或站立，双手推铃过头 — 主练肩部': 'Dumbbell Shoulder Press: seated or standing, press the dumbbells overhead — primarily targets the shoulders',
  '哑铃臀桥：仰卧屈膝，将铃置髋上，顶髋抬起 — 主练臀部': 'Dumbbell Hip Thrust: lie on your back with knees bent, weight on the hips, drive the hips up — primarily targets the glutes',
  '哑铃自然下垂于体侧，掌心朝前，肘关节固定贴身，肩胛下沉，核心收紧，准备肱二头肌发力上弯。': 'Dumbbells hanging naturally at the sides, palms facing forward, elbows fixed at the sides, shoulder blades depressed, core braced, ready to curl with the biceps.',
  '哑铃自然下垂，掌心相对，肘关节固定贴身，肩胛下沉，核心收紧，准备肱二头肌和肱桡肌发力。': 'Dumbbells hanging naturally, palms facing each other, elbows fixed at the sides, shoulder blades depressed, core braced, ready to engage the biceps and brachioradialis.',
  '哑铃起始位于肩前，掌心向内': 'Dumbbells start in front of the shoulders, palms facing in',
  '哑铃顶端不碰撞': 'Don\'t let the dumbbells collide at the top',
  '哑铃飞鸟': 'Dumbbell Fly',
  '哑铃飞鸟重点拉伸胸大肌，增加胸部肌肉的伸展范围，适合作为卧推的辅助动作。': 'The dumbbell flye emphasizes stretching the pecs and increases the range of motion of the chest muscles, making it a good assistance movement for the bench press.',
  '器材选择：杠铃、哑铃与固定器械': 'Equipment Selection: Barbells, Dumbbells, and Machines',
  '器械': 'Machine',
  '器械只是工具，练对部位、练得安全，才是健身的正确打开方式。': 'Equipment is just a tool — training the right muscles, safely, is the right way to approach fitness.',
  '器械：\${t.equipment}': 'Equipment: \${t.equipment}',
  '四': 'Four',
  '四个维度中任意一个停滞超过 3 周，就需要主动调整方案而非死磕。多数塑形瓶颈是恢复不足或营养跟不上，不是训练不够': 'If any of the four dimensions stalls for more than 3 weeks, adjust the plan proactively instead of grinding it out. Most physique plateaus come from insufficient recovery or nutrition lagging behind, not from not training hard enough',
  '四分化': '4-Day Split',
  '四分化训练完全指南': 'The Complete Guide to the 4-Day Split',
  '四大健康支柱': 'The Four Pillars of Health',
  '四种主流高级分化对比': 'Comparison of Four Main Advanced Splits',
  '围度停滞：连续 4 周主要围度（肩/胸/腰/臀/大腿）无变化\n体脂卡点：体脂率连续 3 周不下降，且饮食已严格\n力量平台：主项重量 3 次训练无突破，甚至退步\n视觉无变化：自拍对比 4 周无明显线条差异': 'Measurement stall: no change in key measurements (shoulders/chest/waist/hips/thighs) for 4 consecutive weeks\nBody fat stuck: body fat percentage hasn\'t dropped for 3 weeks despite strict dieting\nStrength plateau: no progress on main lifts for 3 sessions, or even regression\nNo visual change: no obvious difference in progress photos after 4 weeks',
  '固定器械对新手更友好。本章介绍练胸、练背、练肩练臂的经典固定器械，以及它们各自练到的肌群。': 'Machines are more beginner-friendly. This chapter covers the classic machines for chest, back, shoulders, and arms, and the muscles each one works.',
  '固定器械的角色定位': 'The Role of Machines',
  '固定器械通过滑轮和导轨固定运动轨迹，使用者不需要控制平衡，能更专注地感受目标肌群发力。对新手来说，这是建立基础发力模式、熟悉动作路径的极佳工具；对康复期训练者，固定器械提供了低风险环境；对老手而言，固定器械常用于力竭后的 drop set，在杠铃力竭后再切到器械继续榨干目标肌群。但要注意，长期只做固定器械会导致稳定肌发展不足，过渡到自由重量时容易出现代偿或损伤。': 'Machines use pulleys and rails to fix the movement path, so users don\'t have to control balance and can focus more on feeling the target muscle work. For beginners, this is an excellent tool for building basic movement patterns and learning the motion path; for those in rehab, machines provide a low-risk environment; for advanced lifters, machines are often used for drop sets after failure, switching to a machine to fully exhaust the target muscle after barbell failure. Be aware, though, that relying only on machines long term leaves stabilizer muscles underdeveloped, which can lead to compensation or injury when transitioning to free weights.',
  '图文分步教学': 'Step-by-Step Guide with Images',
  '图片解析失败，请重试': 'Failed to parse the image, please try again',
  '在"计划"页面点击右下角 + 号，首次使用会弹出创建引导': 'On the Plans page, tap the + in the bottom right corner; the creation guide will pop up the first time you use it',
  '在"设置 → 计划分享"生成分享码/二维码，好友扫码或粘贴即可导入': 'In Settings → Plan Sharing, generate a share code/QR code; friends can scan or paste it to import',
  '在"设置 → 计划分享"粘贴分享串，或点击"扫码导入"扫描二维码。': 'In Settings → Plan Sharing, paste the share string, or tap Scan to Import to scan a QR code.',
  '在"设置"中调整默认休息时间、组数、次数与重量': 'In Settings, adjust the default rest time, sets, reps, and weight',
  '在「记录邀请成果」中扫码或输入好友的识别码，系统自动校验训练达标与防自邀': 'In Record Invite Results, scan or enter your friend\'s ID code, and the system automatically verifies the training requirement and prevents self-invites',
  '在「输入邀请码」中输入邀请码，激活后立即到账': 'Enter the invite code in Enter Invite Code; rewards are credited immediately after activation',
  '在指定时间推送训练提醒通知': 'Push a training reminder notification at the scheduled time',
  '在笔记详情中标记精选': 'Mark as featured in the note details',
  '地面：铺瑜伽垫，保护关节、防滑\n呼吸：发力（举起）时呼气，还原（放下）时吸气，不屏气\n热身：原地踏步/开合跳 3-5 分钟 + 肩袖绕环\n安排：每周 3 次、每次 30-40 分钟，组间休息 60 秒': 'Floor: lay down a yoga mat to protect joints and prevent slipping\nBreathing: exhale on exertion (lifting), inhale on the way down (lowering), never hold your breath\nWarm-up: 3-5 minutes of marching in place/jumping jacks + shoulder cuff circles\nSchedule: 3 times per week, 30-40 minutes per session, 60 seconds rest between sets',
  '均匀呼吸不憋气': 'Breathe evenly, don\'t hold your breath',
  '坐于划船机上，双脚踩实踏板，膝盖微屈，双手握把手，挺胸收腹，脊柱保持中立位，核心收紧稳定。': 'Sit at the rowing machine, feet firm on the pedals, knees slightly bent, hands on the handle, chest up and abs in, spine neutral, core braced and stable.',
  '坐于哑铃凳（有靠背），双脚踩实，背部贴靠垫，双手持哑铃于肩部两侧，掌心朝前，肘关节略前于躯干。': 'Sit on a dumbbell bench (with backrest), feet flat on the floor, back against the pad, dumbbells at the sides of the shoulders, palms facing forward, elbows slightly in front of the torso.',
  '坐于腿举机，背部紧贴靠垫，双脚与肩同宽放在踏板中上部，脚尖略外展，双手握两侧把手稳定身体。': 'Sit at the leg press, back firmly against the pad, feet shoulder-width apart on the middle-upper part of the platform, toes slightly turned out, hands gripping the side handles to stabilize the body.',
  '坐于高位下拉机，双腿固定压板，双手宽握把手（宽于肩），挺胸收腹，躯干微后倾15度，核心收紧。': 'Sit at the lat pulldown machine, thighs secured under the pads, hands gripping the handle wide (wider than shoulders), chest up and abs in, torso leaning back about 15 degrees, core braced.',
  '坐姿划船': 'Seated Row',
  '坐姿划船重点锻炼背部中部肌群，改善体态和背部厚度。': 'The seated row primarily works the mid-back muscles, improving posture and back thickness.',
  '坐姿屈膝，上身后倾约45度': 'Seated with knees bent, upper body leaning back about 45 degrees',
  '坐姿，单手持哑铃': 'Seated, holding a dumbbell in one hand',
  '坐稳双脚踩实踏板，膝盖微屈': 'Sit firmly with feet on the pedals, knees slightly bent',
  '坚持 · 看到变化': 'Stay Consistent · See the Change',
  '坚持就是力量！连续\$streak天，你正在成为更好的自己。': 'Consistency is strength! \$streak days in a row — you\'re becoming a better version of yourself.',
  '坚持训练': 'Keep Training',
  '坚持，是对自己最好的礼物': 'Consistency is the best gift you can give yourself',
  '坚韧': 'Tenacious',
  '坡度5-8%': 'Incline 5-8%',
  '坡度归零慢走冷身': 'Return the incline to zero and walk slowly to cool down',
  '坡度跑': 'Incline Run',
  '坡度跑1-2分钟后，降低坡度慢跑恢复30-60秒，心率下降后再次提升坡度，交替5-6组。': 'After 1-2 minutes of incline running, lower the incline and jog for 30-60 seconds to recover; once your heart rate drops, raise the incline again, alternating for 5-6 rounds.',
  '坡度跑模拟上坡跑步，强化臀部和股四头肌，同时提升心肺负荷。': 'Incline running simulates running uphill, strengthening the glutes and quadriceps while increasing cardiovascular load.',
  '垂直拉与水平拉比例4:6：水平拉（划船类）对背部厚度（中斜方/菱形/背阔中部）贡献更大应略多': 'Vertical to horizontal pulling ratio of 4:6: horizontal pulls (rows) contribute more to back thickness (mid traps/rhomboids/mid lats), so they should be slightly higher',
  '基于你的信息': 'Based on Your Info',
  '基于训练日历智能调度，7 天内最多 2 次': 'Smart scheduling based on your training calendar, max 2 times in 7 days',
  '基础': 'Basics',
  '基础头像框': 'Basic Avatar Frame',
  '基础操作': 'Basic Operations',
  '基础教学': 'Basic Tutorials',
  '基础数据': 'Basic Data',
  '堡垒': 'Fortress',
  '塑形': 'Toning',
  '塑形与增肌减脂的区别': 'Physique Shaping vs. Bulking and Cutting',
  '塑形后期可采用超级组提升训练密度与代谢压力：二头弯举+三头下压、腿屈伸+腿弯举、侧平举+面拉。超级组延长 TUT 至 40-60 秒，提升生长激素响应，同时节省训练时间。建议每周 1-2 次训练加入超级组，放在训练末段，避免影响复合动作的力量表现。超级组的负荷取 10RM 的 70%，组间休息 75-90 秒。': 'In the later stages of a shaping phase, you can use supersets to increase training density and metabolic stress: biceps curls + triceps pushdowns, leg extensions + leg curls, lateral raises + face pulls. Supersets extend time under tension to 40-60 seconds, boosting the growth hormone response while saving training time. Add supersets to 1-2 sessions per week, placed at the end of the workout to avoid compromising compound lift performance. Use 70% of your 10RM for supersets with 75-90 seconds of rest between them.',
  '塑形是 12-24 个月的长期工程，单次微周期的进步可能微小到肉眼不可见。建议每月对比一次照片与围度，每季度评估一次主项力量。视觉变化往往在连续 8-12 周后才明显显现。坚持记录训练日志、保持营养与睡眠稳定、按周期化推进方案，剩下的交给时间。塑形不是冲刺，而是马拉松式的精雕。': 'Shaping your physique is a 12-24 month long-term project, and progress in a single microcycle may be too small to see with the naked eye. Compare photos and measurements monthly and assess main lift strength quarterly. Visual changes usually become obvious only after 8-12 consecutive weeks. Keep a training log, keep nutrition and sleep consistent, follow the periodized plan, and leave the rest to time. Shaping isn\'t a sprint — it\'s a marathon of fine-tuning.',
  '塑形期不要放弃大重量复合。许多人误以为"轻重量高次数=塑形"，实际上肌肉保留需要 75% 1RM 以上的张力信号': 'Don\'t give up heavy compound lifts during a shaping phase. Many mistakenly believe that light weight and high reps equal shaping, but preserving muscle requires tension signals above 75% 1RM',
  '塑形期优先尝试 4-1-1-1 强调离心节奏，研究显示离心阶段肌肉损伤与生长信号显著强于向心阶段': 'In a shaping phase, try a 4-1-1-1 tempo to emphasize the eccentric; research shows muscle damage and growth signals during the eccentric phase are significantly stronger than in the concentric phase',
  '塑形期每肌群每周 12-16 组是合理区间。胸部 12 组（卧推+上斜+飞鸟）、背部 16 组（垂直拉+水平拉各 8 组）、腿部 14 组（股四头+腘绳各 7 组）、肩部 10 组（前束+中束+后束）、手臂 8 组（二头+三头各 4 组）。容量过低刺激不足，过高则影响恢复。每 4 周评估一次，弱区肌群可加 2-4 组，强区维持或略减。': 'During a shaping phase, 12-16 sets per muscle group per week is a reasonable range. Chest 12 sets (bench press + incline + flyes), back 16 sets (8 vertical pulls + 8 horizontal pulls), legs 14 sets (7 quads + 7 hamstrings), shoulders 10 sets (front + medial + rear delts), arms 8 sets (4 biceps + 4 triceps). Too little volume understimulates; too much impairs recovery. Reassess every 4 weeks — add 2-4 sets for weak areas, maintain or slightly reduce for strong ones.',
  '塑形期节奏方案': 'Tempo Schemes for a Shaping Phase',
  '塑形期身体适应速度快，连续 4 周以上使用相同重量与组数会进入平台。微周期化通过有计划的累加与减量交替，让身体在累加周接受新刺激、在减量周充分恢复，实现螺旋式进步。4 周循环是塑形期的黄金单位——足够长以产生适应、足够短以保持刺激新鲜度。': 'The body adapts quickly during a shaping phase, so using the same weight and sets for more than 4 consecutive weeks leads to a plateau. Micro-periodization alternates planned accumulation and deload so the body receives new stimuli during accumulation weeks and fully recovers during deload weeks, producing spiral-like progress. A 4-week cycle is the gold standard unit for a shaping phase — long enough to produce adaptation, short enough to keep the stimulus fresh.',
  '塑形瓶颈识别：围度停滞、体脂卡点、力量平台。\n\n评估指标：腰臀比、肩腰比、四肢围度差、力量基线。\n\n常见瓶颈成因：训练单调、容量不足、营养不到位、恢复不足。': 'Identifying shaping plateaus: stalled measurements, body fat sticking points, strength plateaus.\n\nAssessment metrics: waist-to-hip ratio, shoulder-to-waist ratio, limb circumference differences, strength baseline.\n\nCommon causes: monotonous training, insufficient volume, poor nutrition, inadequate recovery.',
  '塑形的核心不是单纯追求围度或低体脂，而是肌肉比例与线条的协调。同样的体重，肩腰比 1.6 比 1.2 在视觉上更接近"倒三角"；同样的体脂，腹肌厚度决定能否清晰显形。塑形者需要在保留肌肉的前提下精细管理脂肪，并通过针对性训练调整局部比例——这是中级训练者最常遇到的瓶颈区。': 'The core of shaping isn\'t simply chasing size or low body fat — it\'s coordinating muscle proportions and definition. At the same body weight, a shoulder-to-waist ratio of 1.6 looks far closer to a V-taper than 1.2; at the same body fat level, ab thickness determines whether definition shows. Shapers need to manage fat precisely while preserving muscle, and adjust local proportions through targeted training — the most common bottleneck for intermediate trainees.',
  '塑形者通常已有 6-12 个月训练基础，全身训练的频率已不足以支撑进一步肌肥大。上下肢分化每周 4 次，让每肌群每周获得 2 次高质量刺激，同时保留 48-72 小时恢复窗口。相比五分化（每肌群每周 1 次），上下肢分化在塑形期能提供更稳定的合成信号，避免长时间不刺激导致的肌肉流失风险——这在热量缺口或维持期尤为重要。': 'Shapers usually have 6-12 months of training experience, and full-body sessions no longer provide enough frequency to support further hypertrophy. An upper/lower split with 4 sessions per week gives each muscle group 2 high-quality stimuli per week while preserving a 48-72 hour recovery window. Compared with a 5-day split (once per muscle group per week), an upper/lower split provides a more stable anabolic signal during a shaping phase and avoids the risk of muscle loss from long gaps between stimuli — especially important in a calorie deficit or maintenance phase.',
  '填写计划名称，如"增肌计划""减脂计划"，方便日后区分。': 'Enter a plan name, e.g. Muscle Gain Plan or Fat Loss Plan, so you can tell them apart later.',
  '增肌': 'Muscle Gain',
  '增肌是马拉松不是短跑，坚持比完美计划更重要。': 'Building muscle is a marathon, not a sprint — consistency matters more than a perfect plan.',
  '增肌是马拉松不是短跑，第一次训练的目标不是练趴下，而是让你愿意来第二次。': 'Building muscle is a marathon, not a sprint — the goal of your first session isn\'t to crush yourself, it\'s to make you want to come back for a second.',
  '增肌的本质是肌肉蛋白质合成速率大于分解速率，这需要两个条件：足够的训练刺激和热量盈余。每日摄入比消耗多 300-500 大卡是合理范围，体重每周增 0.25-0.5kg 为宜——增重过快主要是脂肪堆积，反而影响胰岛素敏感性。肌肉合成的速率有上限，自然训练者每月最多增加 0.5-1kg 纯肌肉，超出的体重都是脂肪。急于求成只会让你后期花更多时间减脂。': 'The essence of muscle gain is muscle protein synthesis exceeding breakdown, which requires two conditions: sufficient training stimulus and a calorie surplus. Eating 300-500 calories more than you burn per day is a reasonable range, with weight gain of 0.25-0.5kg per week — gaining faster mostly adds fat and actually hurts insulin sensitivity. The rate of muscle synthesis has an upper limit: natural trainees can gain at most 0.5-1kg of pure muscle per month, and anything beyond that is fat. Rushing only means spending more time dieting later.',
  '增肌：以自由重量复合动作为主（深蹲、卧推、硬拉、划船）+ 固定器械补充\n减脂：复合动作 + 有氧器械（跑步机/椭圆机/划船机）结合\n塑形：中等重量多次数，侧重臀腿与核心\n健康/新手：先固定器械建立发力感，再过渡自由重量': 'Muscle gain: focus on free-weight compound lifts (squat, bench press, deadlift, row) + machines as a supplement\nFat loss: compound lifts + cardio machines (treadmill/elliptical/rowing machine) combined\nShaping: moderate weight and higher reps, emphasizing glutes, legs, and core\nHealth/beginner: start with machines to learn how to engage muscles, then transition to free weights',
  '壶铃摆动': 'Kettlebell Swing',
  '备注': 'Notes',
  '复制分享串': 'Copy Share Code',
  '复制所有数据到剪贴板': 'Copy All Data to Clipboard',
  '复制文本': 'Copy Text',
  '复制群号': 'Copy Group Number',
  '复制识别码': 'Copy ID Code',
  '复制邀请码': 'Copy Invite Code',
  '复制邀请码或生成邀请海报，通过微信/QQ 发给好友。邀请码永久有效': 'Copy your invite code or generate an invite poster and send it to friends via WeChat/QQ. The invite code never expires',
  '复合与孤立的分工': 'The Division of Labor Between Compound and Isolation',
  '复合动作不偷懒': 'No Slacking on Compound Lifts',
  '复合动作优先（深蹲/卧推/硬拉/引体/划船），占训练 70% 以上\n孤立动作补充（弯举/三头下压/侧平举），补足弱区\n不追求动作数量，做精每个动作比堆数量更重要\n热身 5 分钟有氧 + 动态拉伸，激活目标肌群\n放松 5 分钟静态拉伸，重点拉伸训练过的肌群': 'Compound lifts first (squat/bench press/deadlift/pull-up/row), making up 70%+ of training\nIsolation work as a supplement (curls/triceps pushdowns/lateral raises) to fill weak points\nDon\'t chase exercise count — doing each movement well matters more than piling on volume\nWarm up with 5 minutes of cardio + dynamic stretching to activate the target muscles\nCool down with 5 minutes of static stretching, focusing on the muscles trained',
  '复合动作停在技术力竭而非绝对力竭，避免神经系统过度疲劳影响下次训练': 'Stop compound lifts at technical failure rather than absolute failure, to avoid excessive nervous system fatigue affecting your next session',
  '复合动作打底：深蹲/卧推/硬拉/引体/推举，5×6-8 次力量区。\n\n孤立动作精雕：飞鸟/侧平举/腿屈伸/三头下压，3×12-15 次肌肥大区。\n\n弱区专项：上胸、侧束、腘绳肌、腹斜肌，单独加 2-3 组。': 'Compound lifts as the base: squat/bench press/deadlift/pull-up/overhead press, 5×6-8 in the strength range.\n\nIsolation work for detail: flyes/lateral raises/leg extensions/triceps pushdowns, 3×12-15 in the hypertrophy range.\n\nWeak-point specialty work: upper chest, lateral delts, hamstrings, obliques — add 2-3 dedicated sets.',
  '复合动作的选择与负荷': 'Compound Lift Selection and Loading',
  '复合动作至上派': 'Compound-First Devotee',
  '复合动作负责整体围度与力量基础，孤立动作负责线条精雕与弱区补强。塑形期两者比例建议 70:30——复合动作占训练主轴，确保整体肌肉量不流失；孤立动作在复合力竭后补足，针对薄弱区域做精雕。只做复合会留下视觉短板（如侧束平坦、上胸薄弱），只做孤立则缺乏整体厚度支撑。': 'Compound lifts build overall size and the strength foundation, while isolation work refines definition and reinforces weak points. For a shaping phase, a 70:30 ratio is recommended — compounds form the backbone of the program to preserve total muscle mass, while isolation work comes after compound failure to detail weak areas. Compounds alone leave visual gaps (flat lateral delts, weak upper chest); isolation alone lacks overall thickness.',
  '复合变式补足：上斜哑铃替代平板卧推强化上胸\n孤立动作精雕：侧平举 4 组强化中束、腿弯举强化腘绳\n动作角度多样：不同握距/角度刺激不同肌纤维\n负荷曲线匹配：阻力曲线与力量曲线匹配的动作优先\n关节友好优先：长期可持续比短期突破重要': 'Compound variations as a supplement: incline dumbbell press instead of flat barbell bench to target the upper chest\nIsolation for detail: 4 sets of lateral raises for the medial delts, leg curls for the hamstrings\nVary angles: different grips/angles stimulate different muscle fibers\nMatch the loading curve: prioritize exercises whose resistance curve matches the strength curve\nJoint-friendly first: long-term sustainability matters more than short-term PRs',
  '外旋不充分': 'Insufficient external rotation',
  '外食技巧': 'Eating Out Tips',
  '外食时选烤/蒸/煮而非炸，酱料分开蘸能少一半热量。先吃菜再吃肉最后吃主食，可降低血糖波动、增加饱腹感。火锅选清汤锅底，避开丸子类加工食品（多数是淀粉和肥肉）。日料比中餐更适合减脂期——刺身、寿司（少饭）、味噌汤都是不错的选择。聚餐前先吃个鸡蛋或喝杯酸奶垫底，能显著减少外食时的暴食概率。': 'When eating out, choose grilled/steamed/boiled over fried, and get sauce on the side to cut calories in half. Eat vegetables first, then protein, then carbs to reduce blood sugar spikes and increase satiety. For hotpot, pick a clear broth base and avoid processed balls (mostly starch and fat). Japanese food suits a fat-loss phase better than Chinese — sashimi, sushi (light on rice), and miso soup are all solid choices. Eat an egg or drink some yogurt before a gathering to significantly reduce the chance of overeating.',
