  '应用此主题': 'Apply this theme',
  '应用筛选': 'Apply filters',
  '底端停顿': 'Pause at the bottom',
  '底端停顿不弹回': 'Pause at the bottom, no rebound',
  '底端停顿感受拉伸': 'Pause at the bottom and feel the stretch',
  '底端平行': 'Parallel at the bottom',
  '底端悬挂': 'Dead hang at the bottom',
  '底端拉伸': 'Stretch at the bottom',
  '底端收缩': 'Contract at the bottom',
  '底端肩胛不松弛': 'Shoulder blades stay tight at the bottom',
  '底端触胸': 'Touch the chest at the bottom',
  '建立力量根基': 'Build a Strength Foundation',
  '建立可持续的饮食习惯比追求完美更重要。允许 20% 的灵活食物（每周 3-4 餐自由吃），避免非黑即白的思维——一次暴食不代表失败，关键是长期趋势。坚持力量训练维持肌肉量，肌肉是代谢的引擎——同样体重的肌肉比脂肪每天多消耗 6-10 大卡，肌肉量高的人维持期更容易。把减脂视为生活方式的转变，而非一次性的战役。': 'Building sustainable eating habits matters more than chasing perfection. Allow 20% flexible foods (3-4 free meals a week) and avoid all-or-nothing thinking - one binge is not failure, the long-term trend is what counts. Keep lifting to hold on to muscle, because muscle is the engine of your metabolism: at the same body weight, muscle burns 6-10 more kcal per day than fat, so people with more muscle maintain more easily. Treat fat loss as a lifestyle change, not a one-off battle.',
  '建立基线比追求绝对值更重要。每周固定时间（建议周一晨起空腹）测量肩/胸/腰/臀/大腿/上臂围度，拍照正面/侧面/背面三视图。力量基线取主项 5RM：深蹲、卧推、硬拉、推举、引体。这些数据将作为后续 12 周调整方案的锚点，没有基线就无法判断"停滞"是真实发生还是主观错觉。': 'Establishing a baseline matters more than chasing absolute numbers. Measure shoulder/chest/waist/hip/thigh/upper-arm girth at a fixed time each week (Monday morning, fasted, is recommended) and take front/side/back photos. For strength, use a 5RM on the main lifts: squat, bench press, deadlift, overhead press and pull-up. These numbers anchor your adjustments over the next 12 weeks - without a baseline you cannot tell whether a "stall" is real or just in your head.',
  '开卡日期': 'Activation Date',
  '开卡月份': 'Card Activation Month',
  '开合跳': 'Jumping Jacks',
  '开合跳：全身协调，心率提升快，适合热身和恢复\n高抬腿：下肢主导，强化髂腰肌和核心\n波比跳：全身爆发，强度极高，HIIT 之王\n登山者：核心+下肢，心率提升快，对关节冲击小\n战绳：上肢+核心，无冲击，适合关节敏感者': 'Jumping jacks: full-body coordination, raises heart rate fast, good for warm-ups and recovery\nHigh knees: lower-body focused, strengthens the hip flexors and core\nBurpees: full-body explosive power, extremely intense, the king of HIIT\nMountain climbers: core + lower body, raises heart rate fast, low joint impact\nBattle ropes: upper body + core, zero impact, good for sensitive joints',
  '开启「横幅通知」开关': 'Turn on the "Banner Notifications" switch',
