  '引体': 'Pull-up',
  '引体向上': 'Pull-up',
  '引体向上借力摆动（kipping），未做到肩胛骨先下沉后收缩，降低背阔激活': 'Using momentum to swing (kipping) on pull-ups instead of depressing the shoulder blades before contracting, which reduces lat activation',
  '引体向上是背部训练的黄金动作，主要锻炼背阔肌和肱二头肌。': 'The pull-up is the gold-standard back exercise, mainly working the latissimus dorsi and biceps.',
  '引体向上是衡量上肢拉力（背阔肌、二头、小臂）的黄金动作，能同时发展背部宽度和力量。但很多新手一开始做不到完整引体，可从弹力带辅助或高位下拉开始过渡，逐步建立拉力基础。当能做 3 组、每组 6 个标准引体时，你的上肢拉力已经超过健身房 80% 的人。下方是引体向上的详细教程卡。': 'The pull-up is the gold-standard test of upper-body pulling strength (lats, biceps, forearms), building both back width and strength. But many beginners cannot do a full pull-up at first - start with band-assisted pull-ups or lat pulldowns and build a base of pulling strength. Once you can do 3 sets of 6 strict pull-ups, your pulling strength beats 80% of the people in the gym. Below is a detailed pull-up tutorial card.',
  '张力时间（TUT）是肌肥大的重要驱动因素。复合动作单组 TUT 30-40 秒（6-8 次×4-5 秒/次），孤立动作单组 40-60 秒（10-15 次×3-4 秒/次）。塑形期可适当延长 TUT 至 50-70 秒以增加代谢压力，但超过 75 秒会显著降低负荷影响力量保留。建议每周 1-2 次训练采用延长 TUT 的节奏，其余训练保持标准节奏。': 'Time under tension (TUT) is an important driver of hypertrophy. For compound lifts, aim for 30-40 seconds of TUT per set (6-8 reps x 4-5 seconds per rep); for isolation moves, 40-60 seconds per set (10-15 reps x 3-4 seconds per rep). During a shaping phase you can extend TUT to 50-70 seconds for more metabolic stress, but going past 75 seconds significantly reduces the load and hurts strength retention. Use an extended-TUT tempo in 1-2 sessions per week and keep a standard tempo in the rest.',
  '弧线夹拢肘部引导': 'Draw the elbows together along an arc',
  '弧线轨迹下放': 'Lower along an arc',
  '弯举': 'Curl',
  '弯举呼气，下放吸气': 'Exhale as you curl, inhale as you lower',
  '弯举至肩前，顶峰收缩1秒': 'Curl up to shoulder height, hold the peak contraction for 1 second',
  '弯举至肩前，顶峰收缩2秒': 'Curl up to shoulder height, hold the peak contraction for 2 seconds',
  '弱链专项化也需要周期化，避免适应。每 4 周切换一次辅助动作变式：例如上胸第 1-4 周用上斜哑铃卧推、第 5-8 周用上斜杠铃、第 9-12 周用 Hammer Strength 上斜器械。变式切换给目标肌群新的刺激角度，同时降低关节重复负荷。这种轮换是高级者长期突破的关键，比死磕单一动作更有效。每个变式执行 4 周足以建立神经适应并产生肌肥大信号。': 'Weak-point specialization also needs periodization to avoid adaptation. Switch the accessory variation every 4 weeks: for the upper chest, weeks 1-4 incline dumbbell press, weeks 5-8 incline barbell, weeks 9-12 the Hammer Strength incline machine. Rotating variations gives the target muscle new angles of stimulus while reducing repetitive joint loading. This rotation is the key to long-term progress for advanced lifters and beats grinding away at a single exercise. Four weeks per variation is enough to build neural adaptation and produce a hypertrophy signal.',
  '弱链专项化的周期化': 'Periodizing Weak-Point Specialization',
  '弱链是限制整体进步的薄弱环节。诊断方法：①主项力量比例（深蹲:卧推:硬拉应为 1.5:1:1.8，偏离则为弱链）；②视觉评估（拍照对比各肌群发达度）；③力竭测试（同重量下哪个肌群先力竭）。常见弱链：上胸（平板卧推强但上斜弱）、背阔中部（垂直拉强但水平拉弱）、腘绳肌（深蹲强但硬拉弱）、三角肌中束（肩推强但侧平举弱）。精准诊断是辅助专项化的前提。': 'A weak link is the weak point that limits overall progress. How to diagnose: ① main lift ratios (squat : bench : deadlift should be about 1.5 : 1 : 1.8 - deviations point to a weak link); ② visual assessment (compare photos for muscle group development); ③ failure testing (which muscle gives out first at the same load). Common weak links: upper chest (strong flat bench, weak incline), mid lats (strong vertical pull, weak horizontal pull), hamstrings (strong squat, weak deadlift), lateral delts (strong shoulder press, weak lateral raise). Accurate diagnosis is the prerequisite for targeted accessory work.',
  '弱链诊断方法': 'How to Diagnose Weak Links',
  '弱链诊断：胸/背/腿/肩/臂中哪个肌群滞后。\n\n辅助动作选择：针对弱链的孤立+复合变式。\n\n容量分配：主项 60%、辅助 25%、孤立 15%。': 'Weak-link diagnosis: which muscle group is lagging among chest/back/legs/shoulders/arms.\n\nAccessory selection: isolation + compound variations targeting the weak link.\n\nVolume split: 60% main lifts, 25% accessories, 15% isolation.',
  '弱项日安排与主项日相邻，影响大肌群恢复（如弱项手臂日紧接胸部日）': 'Scheduling a weak-point day right next to a main lift day hurts recovery of large muscle groups (for example, an arm weak-point day right after chest day)',
  '强度波动的应用': 'Applying Intensity Fluctuation',
  '强度监控与心率区间': 'Intensity Monitoring and Heart Rate Zones',
  '当你居家训练已经游刃有余、且体验到力量增长带来的成就感时，就可以考虑进健身房系统进阶——更大的器械、更重的重量、更专业的氛围。但请记住：居家训练的坚持能力，永远是你最宝贵的资产，健身房只是它的升级版。': 'When home workouts feel easy and you are hooked on the progress you are making, it is time to move to a gym and level up systematically - bigger equipment, heavier weights, a more professional atmosphere. But remember: the consistency you built at home is always your most valuable asset, and the gym is just its upgrade.',
