  '当前设备暂不支持相机扫码，请从相册选择二维码图片进行识别。': 'This device does not support camera scanning; please pick a QR code image from your album to scan.',
  '当前设备暂不支持相机扫码，请从相册选择二维码图片进行识别导入。': 'This device does not support camera scanning; please pick a QR code image from your album to scan and import.',
  '当前轮次进度': 'Current Round Progress',
  '当前连续': 'Current Streak',
  '当基础动作变轻松，就是进阶的时候。本章教你如何调整训练难度、增加容量，以及何时、如何从居家过渡到健身房。': 'When the basic moves start to feel easy, it is time to progress. This chapter shows you how to adjust training difficulty and add volume, and when and how to transition from home workouts to the gym.',
  '当日无训练记录': 'No training records for this day',
  '当连续 2 个微周期主项无法突破时，可尝试：①动作变式轮换（深蹲→前蹲→暂停深蹲）；②负荷倒退（重量回到 4 周前的水平重新建立）；③频率调整（短期 1 周内增加 1 次专项训练）；④节奏强化（切换 4-1-1-1 节奏 2 周）。这些手段打破身体的预期适应，重新激活进步信号。': 'When a main lift stalls for 2 consecutive microcycles, you can try: ① rotating lift variations (squat → front squat → pause squat); ② load regression (drop back to the weight from 4 weeks ago and rebuild); ③ frequency adjustment (add 1 extra specialty session for 1 week); ④ tempo emphasis (switch to a 4-1-1-1 tempo for 2 weeks). These measures break your body\'s expected adaptation and reactivate the progress signal.',
  '彩霞': 'Sunset Glow',
  '待开始': 'Not Started',
  '很多人在开始健身之旅时，会在家用器械和去健身房之间犹豫。事实上，健身房提供了家用无法替代的优势：完整的器械配置让你能刺激每一块肌肉；训练氛围让你更容易进入状态；更重要的是，镜子里的自己和身旁的训练者，会成为你坚持的动力。本章将带你认识健身房的区域划分、器材分类与基础礼仪，让你第一次走进健身房就能从容不迫。': 'When starting their fitness journey, many people hesitate between home equipment and joining a gym. In fact, gyms offer advantages you cannot replicate at home: a full range of equipment to hit every muscle; an atmosphere that gets you in the zone; and, more importantly, the person in the mirror and the lifters around you become the motivation that keeps you going. This chapter walks you through gym zones, equipment categories and basic etiquette, so your first visit feels completely natural.',
  '很多新手在"要不要办健身卡"上犹豫徘徊。居家训练最大的优势是零门槛——不用通勤、不惧人多、随时可练。它让你把健身的启动成本降到最低，而持续坚持是所有效果的前提。居家训练还能锻炼自律，是建立长期习惯的最佳起点。等你养成了规律训练的习惯，再考虑是否去健身房进阶也不迟。': 'Many beginners go back and forth over "should I get a gym membership". The biggest advantage of home training is zero barrier - no commute, no crowds, train anytime. It keeps the startup cost of fitness as low as possible, and sticking with it is the prerequisite for any result. Home training also builds self-discipline and is the best way to start a long-term habit. Once training is a regular habit, it is not too late to consider joining a gym to level up.',
  '很多新手误以为增肌就是多吃肉，实际上单一营养素过量反而增加肝肾负担、降低吸收效率。一份完整的增肌餐应同时包含蛋白质（鸡胸肉/鱼/蛋）、碳水（米饭/燕麦/红薯）和蔬菜（西兰花/菠菜），三者协同才能让营养真正进入肌肉。优质食物的多样化比单一营养素堆量更重要——饮食越多样，微量元素摄入越均衡，长期训练状态越稳定。': 'Many beginners think building muscle just means eating more meat, but overloading a single nutrient actually burdens the liver and kidneys and lowers absorption efficiency. A complete muscle-building meal includes protein (chicken breast/fish/eggs), carbs (rice/oats/sweet potato) and vegetables (broccoli/spinach) - all three work together to actually deliver nutrients into muscle. Variety in quality foods matters more than piling up one nutrient: the more varied your diet, the more balanced your micronutrient intake and the more stable your long-term training performance.',
  '循环重复': 'Repeat the circuit',
  '微信/QQ/复制': 'WeChat / QQ / Copy',
  '微信群': 'WeChat Group',
  '微周期：4 周为一循环，3 周累加 + 1 周减量。\n\n累加周：每周主项 +2.5kg（上肢）/+5kg（下肢），辅助加 1 组。\n\n减量周：重量降至 70%，组数减半，主动恢复。': 'Microcycle: a 4-week loop with 3 loading weeks + 1 deload week.\n\nLoading weeks: add +2.5 kg (upper body) / +5 kg (lower body) to main lifts each week, plus 1 extra accessory set.\n\nDeload week: drop the weight to 70%, halve the sets, and focus on active recovery.',
  '微曲手肘，固定角度': 'Keep a slight bend in the elbow and lock the angle in place',
  '微曲肘部，抬至与肩平齐': 'Keep a slight bend in the elbow and raise to shoulder height',
  '德州法（Texas Method）：周一5×5容量日/周三2×5恢复日/周五1×5新PR强度日，每周一次PR适合中级力量': 'Texas Method: Monday 5x5 volume day / Wednesday 2x5 recovery day / Friday 1x5 new-PR intensity day - one PR per week, suited to intermediate lifters',
  '徽章': 'Badges',
  '心情贴纸': 'Mood Sticker',
  '心率不超70%': 'Keep heart rate under 70%',
  '心率降至60-70%': 'Heart rate drops to 60-70%',
  '心肺': 'Cardio',
  '心肺功能对健康的核心价值': 'Why Cardiorespiratory Fitness Is Core to Health',
  '心肺功能是预测全因死亡率的最强独立指标，超过吸烟、糖尿病、高血压。研究显示，最大摄氧量（VO2max）每提高 3.5 ml/kg/min，心血管疾病死亡风险降低 10-15%。力量训练对心肺的刺激有限，必须配合专门的有氧训练。健康训练者不应忽视有氧，把它视为与力量同等重要的健康支柱。': 'Cardiorespiratory fitness is the strongest independent predictor of all-cause mortality, stronger than smoking, diabetes or high blood pressure. Research shows that every 3.5 ml/kg/min increase in VO2max lowers cardiovascular death risk by 10-15%. Strength training provides limited cardiovascular stimulus, so dedicated cardio is a must. Healthy trainees should not neglect cardio - treat it as a health pillar just as important as strength.',
  '必填': 'Required',
  '快走是最易坚持的有氧形式，适合初学者和恢复日；心率提升慢但关节冲击极低。骑行（户外或室内）对下肢力量有补充作用，心率提升快、冲击低。游泳是全身有氧，对关节零冲击，但需要游泳技能。椭圆机是健身房的低冲击首选，心率提升快且可调节阻力。建议根据个人条件选择 1-2 种作为长期有氧形式，避免单一形式导致枯燥。': 'Brisk walking is the easiest cardio to stick with, good for beginners and recovery days; heart rate rises slowly and joint impact is minimal. Cycling (outdoor or indoor) complements lower-body strength, raises heart rate quickly and is low impact. Swimming is a full-body cardio option with zero joint impact, but it requires swimming skills. The elliptical is the top low-impact choice at the gym, with a fast heart rate response and adjustable resistance. Pick 1-2 forms that suit your situation and stick with them long term to avoid boredom from doing only one.',
  '忽略': 'Ignore',
  '忽视deload周设计，持续高强度训练导致过度训练综合征（睡眠差/表现退步/免疫力降）': 'Ignoring deload week programming; continuous high-intensity training leads to overtraining syndrome (poor sleep, declining performance, lower immunity)',
  '忽视下背部（竖脊肌）训练，只练背阔肌导致上背发达下背薄弱，应加山羊挺身/硬拉变式': 'Neglecting lower back (erector spinae) training, working only the lats and ending up with a developed upper back but a weak lower back - add back extensions/deadlift variations',
  '忽视减量周（Deload），持续高强度训练导致过度训练综合征': 'Ignoring deload weeks; continuous high-intensity training leads to overtraining syndrome',
  '忽视恢复（睡眠<7小时/蛋白质<1.6g/kg）使RPE虚高，误判为力量平台': 'Neglecting recovery (sleep <7 hours / protein <1.6 g/kg) inflates RPE and makes it look like a strength plateau',
  '忽视核心训练，仅安排在腿日末尾草草了事，应每周独立2次8-12分钟核心训练': 'Neglecting core training, only tacking it on at the end of leg day - do dedicated core work twice a week for 8-12 minutes',
  '忽视热身': 'Skipping the warm-up',
  '忽视离心控制（下放过快<1秒），失去50%以上的肌肉机械张力刺激': 'Neglecting eccentric control (lowering faster than 1 second) loses more than 50% of the mechanical tension stimulus',
  '忽视肱肌训练（锤式弯举/反握弯举），肱肌位于肱二头肌下方，增厚可推高二头视觉围度': 'Neglecting the brachialis (hammer curls/reverse curls); the brachialis sits under the biceps, and thickening it pushes up visual arm size',
  '忽视辅助肌群训练': 'Neglecting accessory muscle groups',
