  '权限已授予': 'Permission Granted',
  '权限管理': 'Permission Management',
  '杠铃': 'Barbell',
  '杠铃/哑铃': 'Barbell/Dumbbell',
  '杠铃/哑铃/器械': 'Barbell/Dumbbell/Machine',
  '杠铃/哑铃/绳索': 'Barbell/Dumbbell/Cable',
  '杠铃/哑铃/绳索/单杠': 'Barbell/Dumbbell/Cable/Pull-up Bar',
  '杠铃下放至上胸部': 'Lower the barbell to the upper chest',
  '杠铃与哑铃的区别与选择。\n\n杠铃：适合大重量复合动作（深蹲、卧推、硬拉），能加载更大重量。\n\n哑铃：适合单侧训练和修正不平衡，活动范围更自由。\n\n固定器械：轨迹固定，安全性高，适合新手建立基础发力模式。\n\n安全提示：杠铃训练必须有保护杠或搭档保护，使用安全锁扣固定杠铃片。': 'Barbell vs. Dumbbell: differences and how to choose.\n\nBarbell: best for heavy compound lifts (squat, bench press, deadlift) — it can load the most weight.\n\nDumbbell: ideal for unilateral work and fixing imbalances, with a freer range of motion.\n\nMachines: fixed path, high safety, great for beginners building basic force production patterns.\n\nSafety note: barbell training requires safety bars or a spotter, and always secure the plates with collars.',
  '杠铃与哑铃的本质区别': 'The Essential Difference Between Barbells and Dumbbells',
  '杠铃位于膝盖下方': 'Barbell below the knees',
  '杠铃位于锁骨正上方': 'Barbell directly above the collarbone',
  '杠铃划': 'Barbell Row',
  '杠铃划船': 'Barbell Row',
  '杠铃划船全面刺激背部肌群，特别是背阔肌中下部和菱形肌。': 'The barbell row works the entire back, especially the mid and lower lats and the rhomboids.',
  '杠铃卧推': 'Barbell Bench Press',
  '杠铃卧推和杠铃深蹲是增肌训练的两大基础复合动作：卧推发展胸、肩、三头，深蹲发展股四头、臀、核心。建议在专业教练指导下先用空杆学习标准动作模式，重点掌握握距、站距、脊柱中立、呼吸与发力路径，再逐步加重量。空杆阶段不要觉得没面子——许多顶尖力量举运动员每周依然会用空杆做技术热身。每周 1-2 次、每次 4-6 组、每组 5-8 次，是力量与围度的经典安排。除卧推和深蹲外，硬拉、划船、推举也值得长期打磨，覆盖全身主要肌群构成完整训练骨架。下方是卧推和深蹲两个动作的详细教程卡，点击查看完整要点。': 'The barbell bench press and the barbell back squat are the two foundational compound lifts for building muscle: the bench press develops the chest, shoulders, and triceps, while the squat develops the quads, glutes, and core. Work with a qualified coach to learn the standard movement patterns with an empty bar first — focus on grip width, stance width, a neutral spine, breathing, and the path of force — then add weight gradually. Do not be embarrassed about the empty-bar phase: many top powerlifters still warm up technically with an empty bar every week. 1-2 sessions per week, 4-6 sets per session, 5-8 reps per set is the classic setup for strength and size. Beyond bench and squat, the deadlift, row, and overhead press also deserve long-term refinement — together they cover all major muscle groups and form a complete training skeleton. Below are detailed tutorial cards for the bench press and the squat; tap to see the full key points.',
  '杠铃和哑铃是自由重量训练的两大核心工具，但它们各有侧重。杠铃采用双手握持的对称结构，能加载极大重量，对神经肌肉系统的募集刺激最强，特别适合深蹲、卧推、硬拉这类多关节复合动作，是力量和围度增长的首选工具。哑铃则活动范围更自由，允许手腕和肘部自然转动，对关节更友好，能单侧训练以修正左右不平衡，适合作为杠铃动作的补充或某些动作的替代。两者并非替代关系，而是互补——好的训练计划会同时使用杠铃和哑铃。': 'Barbells and dumbbells are the two core tools of free-weight training, but each has its strengths. The barbell\'s two-handed, symmetrical structure can load very heavy weights and produces the strongest neuromuscular recruitment, making it ideal for multi-joint compound lifts like the squat, bench press, and deadlift — the top tool for strength and size. Dumbbells allow a freer range of motion and natural rotation at the wrist and elbow, making them easier on the joints; they allow unilateral training to correct left-right imbalances and work well as a supplement to — or replacement for — certain barbell movements. They are not substitutes for each other; they are complements. A good program uses both.',
  '杠铃悬垂于膝盖下方，手臂自然伸直，肩胛放松下沉，背部平直，重心在足中，准备背部发力上拉。': 'The barbell hangs below the knees, arms naturally straight, shoulder blades relaxed and depressed, back flat, weight over mid-foot, ready to pull with the back.',
  '杠铃拉至下腹位置，肩胛充分后缩，背阔肌顶峰收缩1秒，控制下放，完成一次重复，保持背部平直。': 'Pull the barbell to the lower abdomen with full scapular retraction, hold the lat peak contraction for 1 second, lower under control to complete one rep, keeping the back flat.',
  '杠铃推举': 'Barbell Overhead Press',
  '杠铃深蹰': 'Barbell Squat',
  '杠铃深蹲': 'Barbell Squat',
  '杠铃置于前三角肌与锁骨之间': 'Barbell resting between the front delts and the collarbone',
  '杠铃置于斜方肌上沿': 'Barbell resting on the upper traps',
  '杠铃置于斜方肌上沿（高杠位），双脚与肩同宽，脚尖略外展15-30度，挺胸收腹，核心收紧，肘部下压。': 'Barbell resting on the upper traps (high bar position), feet shoulder-width apart, toes turned out 15-30 degrees, chest up and abs drawn in, core braced, elbows pulled down.',
  '杠铃置于斜方肌上部（高杠）': 'Barbell on the upper traps (high bar)',
  '杠铃置于锁骨前，握距略宽于肩': 'Barbell in front of the collarbone, grip slightly wider than shoulder width',
  '杠铃训练必须有保护杠或搭档保护，使用安全锁扣固定杠铃片，避免脱手或一侧滑落造成严重伤害': 'Barbell training requires safety bars or a spotter, and plates must be secured with collars to keep the bar from slipping out of your hands or plates sliding off one side and causing serious injury',
  '杠铃贴大腿前侧': 'Barbell against the front of the thighs',
  '杠铃贴身拉至下腹': 'Pull the barbell close to the body up to the lower abdomen',
  '杠铃轨迹垂直于肩关节正上方': 'Bar path vertical, directly above the shoulder joint',
  '杠铃轨迹垂直向上': 'Bar path straight up',
  '杠铃轻触胸部后停顿0.5-1秒，不反弹借力，臀部不离凳，双脚不挪动，保持肩胛稳定，准备发力推起。': 'After the barbell lightly touches the chest, pause 0.5-1 second — no bouncing or momentum; hips stay on the bench, feet stay planted, shoulder blades stay stable, ready to drive the bar up.',
  '杠铃远离身体': 'Bar drifting away from the body',
  '杠铃适合大重量复合动作（深蹲、卧推、硬拉），能加载更大重量，对神经肌肉系统的刺激最强，是力量和围度增长的首选工具。哑铃适合单侧训练和修正左右不平衡，活动范围更自由，对关节更友好，适合作为杠铃动作的补充或替代。固定器械轨迹固定、安全性高，适合新手建立基础发力模式、康复期训练或力竭后的 drop set。三者并非互相替代，而是根据训练阶段和目标灵活组合。': 'Barbells suit heavy compound lifts (squat, bench press, deadlift); they load the most weight and deliver the strongest neuromuscular stimulus, making them the top tool for strength and size. Dumbbells suit unilateral work and fixing left-right imbalances; the freer range of motion is easier on the joints, so they work well as a supplement to or replacement for barbell movements. Machines have a fixed path and high safety, suiting beginners building basic force patterns, rehab training, or drop sets after failure. The three do not replace one another — combine them flexibly based on your training phase and goals.',
  '杠铃锁定于肩关节正上方': 'Barbell locked out directly above the shoulder joint',
