  '热身准备': 'Warm-up',
  '热身：5-10 分钟动态热身 + 动作专项激活。\n\n安全：动作标准优于速度、力竭时停止、监测心率。\n\n进阶：每 4 周加 1 个循环或缩短休息，避免突然加量。': 'Warm-up: 5-10 minutes of dynamic warm-up plus movement-specific activation.\n\nSafety: form over speed, stop at failure, monitor heart rate.\n\nProgression: every 4 weeks add 1 round or shorten rest; avoid sudden jumps in volume.',
  '热身：开合跳 + 关节绕环 5 分钟\n训练（每个动作 3 组，组间休息 60 秒）\n  1. 哑铃深蹲 12-15 次\n  2. 哑铃卧推 10-12 次\n  3. 俯身哑铃划船 12 次\n  4. 哑铃肩上推举 10-12 次\n  5. 罗马尼亚硬拉 10-12 次\n  6. 哑铃箭步蹲 每侧 10 次\n  7. 哑铃臀桥 15 次\n  8. 俄罗斯转体 20 次\n放松：静态拉伸 5 分钟': 'Warm-up: jumping jacks + joint circles, 5 minutes\nWorkout (3 sets per exercise, 60 seconds rest between sets)\n  1. Dumbbell squat 12-15 reps\n  2. Dumbbell bench press 10-12 reps\n  3. Bent-over dumbbell row 12 reps\n  4. Dumbbell overhead press 10-12 reps\n  5. Romanian deadlift 10-12 reps\n  6. Dumbbell lunge 10 reps per side\n  7. Dumbbell hip thrust 15 reps\n  8. Russian twist 20 reps\nCool-down: 5 minutes of static stretching',
  '热量盈余的核心原理': 'The Core Principle of a Caloric Surplus',
  '热量盈余：每日摄入比消耗多300-500大卡，体重每周增0.25-0.5kg为宜。\n\n蛋白质：每公斤体重1.6-2.2克，分散到4-5餐摄入。\n\n碳水：训练前后补充碳水，提供训练能量并促进恢复。\n\n脂肪：占总热量20-30%，优选不饱和脂肪。\n\n补水：每日2-3升水，训练时少量多次补充。': 'Caloric surplus: eat 300-500 kcal more than you burn daily, aiming for 0.25-0.5kg of body weight gain per week.\n\nProtein: 1.6-2.2 grams per kg of body weight, spread across 4-5 meals.\n\nCarbs: take them around training to fuel the session and support recovery.\n\nFat: 20-30% of total calories, favoring unsaturated fats.\n\nHydration: 2-3 liters of water daily, sipping small amounts during training.',
  '热量缺口过大（>500大卡/天）导致训练表现下降与肌肉流失，建议300-500大卡赤字': 'Too large a caloric deficit (>500 kcal/day) hurts training performance and causes muscle loss; a 300-500 kcal deficit is recommended',
  '热门推荐': 'Popular',
  '熔炉深蹲': 'Furnace Squat',
  '熔铁匠人': 'Molten Iron Smith',
  '燃力': 'Blaze Power',
  '燃烧': 'Burning',
  '燕麦饱腹感强、GI 低，β-葡聚糖有助于控制血糖。糙米比白米多 3 倍纤维和 B 族维生素。红薯富含 β-胡萝卜素和膳食纤维，甜度适中。全麦面包比白面包 GI 低，但要警惕伪全麦产品（看配料表第一位是否是全麦粉）。土豆饱腹感指数最高，蒸煮方式最佳，油炸或做成土豆泥会显著提升热量与 GI。': 'Oats are very filling with a low GI, and their beta-glucan helps control blood sugar. Brown rice has 3x the fiber and B vitamins of white rice. Sweet potatoes are rich in beta-carotene and fiber with moderate sweetness. Whole wheat bread has a lower GI than white bread, but watch out for fake whole wheat products (check that whole wheat flour is the first ingredient). Potatoes rank highest on the satiety index and are best steamed or boiled — frying or mashing them significantly raises calories and GI.',
  '爆炸': 'Explosive',
  '版本 1.0.0': 'Version 1.0.0',
  '版本 1.0.1': 'Version 1.0.1',
  '牛油果（每半个 15g 脂肪、160 大卡），单不饱和脂肪丰富\n坚果（杏仁/核桃每天 30g），富含镁和维生素 E\n橄榄油（凉拌或低温烹饪），避免高温破坏营养\n鱼油（EPA+DHA 每日 2-3g），降低炎症、保护心血管\n亚麻籽（富含 ALA），研磨后食用更易吸收': 'Avocado (15g fat, 160 kcal per half), rich in monounsaturated fat\nNuts (30g of almonds/walnuts per day), rich in magnesium and vitamin E\nOlive oil (for dressings or low-heat cooking); avoid high heat that destroys nutrients\nFish oil (2-3g of EPA+DHA daily) to lower inflammation and protect cardiovascular health\nFlaxseed (rich in ALA); grind before eating for better absorption',
  '状态信息': 'Status Info',
  '狂风': 'Fierce Wind',
  '猛虎': 'Fierce Tiger',
  '现代健身房通常划分为四大区域。器械区（固定器械）轨迹固定、安全性高，适合新手建立基础发力感，是入门前两周的主要训练区域。自由重量区（杠铃、哑铃）活动范围自由、对稳定肌要求更高，是增肌训练的核心区域，适合掌握基础动作模式后使用。有氧区（跑步机、椭圆机、划船机）主要用于热身和减脂，建议训练前做 5-10 分钟轻度有氧提升体温。力量区（深蹲架、卧推架、硬拉台）是大重量复合动作的专属区域，使用时务必有保护杠或搭档保护。': 'Modern gyms are usually divided into four areas. The machine area (fixed machines) has a fixed path and high safety, making it ideal for beginners developing a basic feel for force production — the main area for your first two weeks. The free weights area (barbells, dumbbells) allows a free range of motion and demands more from the stabilizers; it is the core area for muscle gain, best used after you have mastered basic movement patterns. The cardio area (treadmills, ellipticals, rowing machines) is mainly for warm-ups and fat loss — 5-10 minutes of light cardio before training helps raise body temperature. The strength area (squat racks, bench press racks, deadlift platforms) is dedicated to heavy compound lifts; always use safety bars or a spotter there.',
  '理所当然': 'As It Should Be',
  '瓦式呼吸的原理': 'The Principle of the Valsalva Maneuver',
  '瓦式呼吸的适用范围': 'When to Use the Valsalva Maneuver',
  '瓦式呼吸适用于复合动作（深蹲/卧推/硬拉/推举）的大重量组，不适用于孤立动作或高次数组。在 5 次以下的力训组中，每次重复都独立完成一次瓦式呼吸（顶部换气）。在 8 次以上的肌肥大组中，可采用 2-3 次重复换一次气，避免长时间憋气导致血压升高头晕。瓦式呼吸会短暂升高血压，高血压患者、孕妇应避免，改用连续呼吸。': 'The Valsalva maneuver suits heavy sets of compound lifts (squat/bench press/deadlift/overhead press), not isolation exercises or high-rep sets. In sets of 5 reps or fewer, perform a full Valsalva for each rep (breathing at the top). In hypertrophy sets of 8+ reps, breathe every 2-3 reps to avoid dizziness from prolonged breath holding and rising blood pressure. The Valsalva briefly raises blood pressure, so people with hypertension and pregnant women should avoid it and breathe continuously instead.',
  '瓦式呼吸（Valsalva Maneuver）是力量训练的核心呼吸技术：动作前深吸气到腹部（不是胸腔），屏气并主动收紧腹肌如防御拳击，维持腹内压完成一次重复，回到顶部后吐气。腹内压像气柱一样支撑脊柱，显著降低椎间盘负荷。研究显示，正确瓦式呼吸下脊柱伸肌需求降低 30-40%。这就是为什么大重量训练者必须掌握瓦式呼吸。': 'The Valsalva maneuver is the core breathing technique of strength training: before the lift, take a deep breath into the belly (not the chest), hold it, and actively brace the abs as if bracing for a punch to the gut; maintain intra-abdominal pressure through the rep, then exhale once you are back at the top. Intra-abdominal pressure supports the spine like an air column, significantly reducing disc load. Research shows that with a proper Valsalva, spinal erector demand drops 30-40%. That is why anyone training heavy must master it.',
  '瓦式呼吸：深吸气到腹部+屏气+腹肌加压，完成一次重复后吐气。\n\n核心加压三步：吸气-屏气-收紧腹肌如防御拳击。\n\n禁忌：高血压/孕期避免瓦式，改用连续呼吸。': 'Valsalva maneuver: deep breath into the belly + hold + brace the abs, then exhale after completing a rep.\n\nThree steps of core bracing: inhale - hold - brace the abs as if bracing for a punch.\n\nContraindications: avoid the Valsalva if you have high blood pressure or are pregnant; breathe continuously instead.',
