  '睡眠——健康训练的基石': 'Sleep — The Foundation of Healthy Training',
  '睡眠是健康训练的基石，重要性超过训练本身。深睡期生长激素分泌达峰值、肌肉蛋白合成加速、皮质醇水平降低、记忆与学习整合。30 岁后深睡比例从 25% 降至 15-20%，更需要主动优化睡眠。建议：固定作息、卧室温度 18-20°C、睡前 1 小时无蓝光、避免下午 2 点后摄入咖啡因、晚餐不晚于睡前 3 小时。睡眠不足时主动减量训练，而非强撑。': 'Sleep is the foundation of healthy training — more important than training itself. During deep sleep, growth hormone secretion peaks, muscle protein synthesis accelerates, cortisol drops, and memory and motor learning consolidate. After age 30, the share of deep sleep falls from 25% to 15-20%, so optimizing sleep takes active effort. Recommendations: keep a fixed schedule, bedroom temperature 18-20°C, no blue light for 1 hour before bed, no caffeine after 2pm, and dinner no later than 3 hours before bed. When sleep is insufficient, actively reduce training volume rather than pushing through.',
  '睡眠是最重要的恢复手段': 'Sleep Is the Most Important Recovery Tool',
  '睡眠：每晚7-9小时，肌肉在睡眠中修复生长。\n\n主动恢复：休息日做轻度有氧或拉伸，促进血液循环。\n\n deload周：每4-6周安排一次减量周，重量降至平时的60%，让身体充分恢复。\n\n进阶方向：完成本课程后，可学习分化训练（推拉腿）、力量计划（5x5）等进阶内容。\n\n记住：增肌是马拉松不是短跑，坚持比完美计划更重要。': 'Sleep: 7-9 hours per night; muscles repair and grow while you sleep.\n\nActive recovery: do light cardio or stretching on rest days to promote circulation.\n\nDeload week: every 4-6 weeks, take a deload week and drop the weight to 60% of normal so the body fully recovers.\n\nNext steps: after this course, you can move on to advanced topics like split training (push/pull/legs) and strength programs (5x5).\n\nRemember: building muscle is a marathon, not a sprint — consistency matters more than a perfect plan.',
  '知道了': 'Got It',
  '破晓': 'Daybreak',
  '破浪': 'Wave Breaker',
  '硬拉': 'Deadlift',
  '硬拉技术要点': 'Deadlift Technique Essentials',
  '硬拉起始髋位置决定背部需求：传统硬拉躯干前倾大→脊柱伸肌需求高；相扑硬拉髋外展使躯干直立→背部需求降': 'Starting hip position determines back demand in the deadlift: a conventional deadlift has a more forward-leaning torso → higher spinal erector demand; a sumo deadlift uses hip abduction to keep the torso upright → lower back demand',
  '硬拉起把时膝盖过杠铃前方导致髋后移、瞬时增加髋伸需求，应保持杠铃贴近胫骨': 'On the deadlift pull, letting the knees drift past the bar pushes the hips back and instantly raises hip extension demand — keep the bar close to the shins',
  '硬拉进阶技巧': 'Advanced Deadlift Techniques',
  '硬核': 'Hardcore',
