  '线性进阶不会永远持续。当某个重量连续 3 次训练无法完成规定次数（如深蹲 100kg 3×5，三次训练都无法完成 5×5），说明已进入平台。此时减重 10% 重新开始线性爬升——例如深蹲卡在 100kg，减至 90kg 重新加重。减重后身体在更轻重量的恢复中适应，往往能突破之前的卡点。这是 LP 的"重启"机制，不是失败。': 'Linear progression doesn\'t last forever. When you fail to complete the prescribed reps at a given weight for 3 sessions in a row (e.g. squat 100kg 3×5 and you can\'t finish 5×5 three sessions running), you\'ve hit a plateau. At that point, drop the weight 10% and start the linear climb again — for example, if you\'re stuck at 100kg, drop to 90kg and work back up. The lighter load lets your body recover and adapt, and you\'ll often break past the previous sticking point. This is the "reset" mechanism of LP, not a failure.',
  '线性进阶的基本逻辑': 'The Basic Logic of Linear Progression',
  '线性进阶（LP）→ 周期化（5/3/1）→ 自调节（RPE/DUP）三阶段切换时机：连续3次同重量失败': 'Linear Progression (LP) → Periodization (5/3/1) → Auto-Regulation (RPE/DUP): when to switch between the three stages — failing the same weight 3 sessions in a row',
  '线性进阶（LP）：Starting Strength 3×5/StrongLifts 5×5，每次+2.5-5kg，连续3次失败减重10%重爬，适合零基础': 'Linear Progression (LP): Starting Strength 3×5 / StrongLifts 5×5, add 2.5-5kg each session; after 3 consecutive failures, drop the weight 10% and climb again. Great for complete beginners',
  '线性进阶（Linear Progression, LP）是初学者最有效的力量增长方法。每次训练主项加 2.5kg（上肢：卧推/推举/划船）或 5kg（下肢：深蹲/硬拉），3 组×5 次为标准训练组。这种简单的加重策略能持续提供渐进超负荷，初学者前 8-12 周可线性增加 30-50% 的力量。StrongLifts 5×5 和 Starting Strength 是经典 LP 方案。': 'Linear Progression (LP) is the most effective way for beginners to build strength. Add 2.5kg to each main lift every session (upper body: bench press/press/row) or 5kg (lower body: squat/deadlift), with 3 sets × 5 reps as the standard working sets. This simple loading strategy keeps delivering progressive overload, and beginners can increase strength linearly by 30-50% over the first 8-12 weeks. StrongLifts 5×5 and Starting Strength are classic LP programs.',
  '线性进阶：每次训练主项 +2.5kg（上肢）/+5kg（下肢）。\n\n3 次失败规则：同重量连续 3 次失败，减重 10% 重新爬升。\n\n训练频率：每周 3 次全身训练（A/B/A-B 交替）。': 'Linear progression: +2.5kg (upper body) / +5kg (lower body) on the main lift each session.\n\n3-failure rule: after 3 consecutive failures at the same weight, drop the weight 10% and climb again.\n\nTraining frequency: 3 full-body sessions per week (alternating A/B/A-B).',
