  '肌群分布': 'Muscle Group Distribution',
  '肌肉': 'Muscle',
  '肌肉只在被迫适应新刺激时才会增长。每周尝试增加重量（1-2.5kg）或次数或组数，是渐进超负荷的三大手段。进步不会线性发生，但长期趋势应向上。遇到停滞时优先检查睡眠（是否 7 小时以上）、饮食（蛋白和总热量是否达标）、恢复（是否训练过度），而不是盲目加量。一段时间的退步往往是恢复不足的信号，主动减量一周胜过死磕。': 'Muscle only grows when it\'s forced to adapt to a new stimulus. Adding weight (1-2.5kg), reps or sets each week is the three main tools of progressive overload. Progress isn\'t linear, but the long-term trend should be upward. When you stall, first check sleep (are you getting 7+ hours), nutrition (are protein and total calories on target) and recovery (are you overtraining), rather than blindly adding volume. A stretch of regression is often a sign of under-recovery — taking a deliberate deload week beats grinding it out.',
  '肌肉增长中，离目标越来越近！💪': 'Muscle is growing — you\'re getting closer to your goal! 💪',
  '肌肥大三大机制：机械张力、肌肉损伤、代谢压力。高级者机械张力的增长趋缓（力量进步慢），代谢压力成为重要的补充刺激。代谢压力通过延长 TUT、缩短组间休息、高次数累积代谢产物（乳酸、氢离子、生长激素），激活肌肥大信号通路。研究显示，代谢压力训练能提升生长激素水平 200-400%，对肌肥大有显著补充作用。但滥用会导致过度训练，必须周期化应用。': 'The three mechanisms of hypertrophy: mechanical tension, muscle damage and metabolic stress. For advanced lifters, mechanical tension grows more slowly (strength gains slow down), so metabolic stress becomes an important supplementary stimulus. Metabolic stress accumulates metabolites (lactate, hydrogen ions, growth hormone) by extending time under tension, shortening rest intervals and using higher reps, activating hypertrophic signaling pathways. Research shows metabolic stress training can raise growth hormone levels by 200-400%, making a significant supplementary contribution to hypertrophy. But overusing it leads to overtraining, so it must be applied in a periodized way.',
  '肌肥大周期化中强度不应线性累加，而应波动。例如第 1 周 75%、第 2 周 77.5%、第 3 周降回 75% 但容量加 2 组、第 4 周减量。这种波动避免神经疲劳累积，同时持续提供肌肥大刺激。研究显示，波动式周期化在肌肥大效果上优于纯线性周期化 15-20%。关键是每周都有"刺激-适应"的明确目标，而不是盲目加重。': 'In hypertrophy periodization, intensity shouldn\'t accumulate linearly — it should fluctuate. For example, week 1 at 75%, week 2 at 77.5%, week 3 back down to 75% but with 2 more sets, week 4 a deload. This fluctuation prevents the accumulation of neural fatigue while continuously providing a hypertrophy stimulus. Research shows undulating periodization outperforms purely linear periodization for hypertrophy by 15-20%. The key is that every week has a clear "stimulus-adaptation" goal rather than blindly adding weight.',
