  '训练统计': 'Workout Stats',
  '训练者常见的过度训练信号包括：晨起静息心率上升 5-10 次、握力下降、训练动力降低、睡眠质量变差、小伤口恢复变慢、易感冒。出现这些信号时不要硬撑，主动减量一周胜过死磕一个月。记录每日晨起心率是简单有效的监测手段——长期趋势上升意味着恢复不足，需要立即安排 deload 或彻底休息。营养和睡眠的同步优化，比加练更能突破瓶颈。': 'Common overtraining signals in lifters include: morning resting heart rate up 5-10 beats, decreased grip strength, lower drive to train, poorer sleep quality, slower healing of small wounds, and catching colds more easily. When these show up, don\'t tough it out — a proactive down week beats grinding for a month. Logging your morning heart rate every day is a simple and effective way to monitor: a rising long-term trend means under-recovery and you need to schedule a deload or complete rest right away. Optimizing nutrition and sleep together breaks plateaus better than adding more training.',
  '训练节奏用四位数字表示：离心（下放）- 底部停顿 - 向心（推起）- 顶峰停顿。例如 3-1-1-1 表示 3 秒下放、底部停 1 秒、1 秒推起、顶峰收缩 1 秒，单次动作 6 秒。塑形期通过延长节奏增加张力时间（TUT），在不加重量的前提下提升肌肉刺激，是突破平台的有效手段。': 'Training tempo is written as four digits: eccentric (lowering) - pause at the bottom - concentric (lifting) - pause at the top. For example, 3-1-1-1 means 3 seconds lowering, 1 second pause at the bottom, 1 second lifting, and a 1-second squeeze at the top — 6 seconds per rep. In a shaping phase, slowing the tempo increases time under tension (TUT) and raises muscle stimulus without adding weight, making it an effective way to break a plateau.',
  '训练计划': 'Training Plan',
  '训练计划 · PLAN': 'Training Plan · PLAN',
  '训练记录': 'Workout Records',
  '训练记录海报': 'Workout Record Poster',
  '训练设置': 'Workout Settings',
  '训练详情': 'Workout Details',
  '训练量偏大': 'High Training Volume',
  '训练频率': 'Training Frequency',
  '训练频率不是越多越好，而是要匹配身体的恢复能力。新手建议每周 3 次全身训练（如周一三五），每次覆盖大肌群；进阶者可选上下肢分化每周 4 次，给每个肌群更高容量刺激。频率比单次容量更重要——肌肉蛋白合成信号在训练后 24-48 小时达到峰值，规律刺激才能持续增长。两次训练同一肌群的间隔不应超过 72 小时，否则合成信号衰减，影响长期进步。': 'Training frequency isn\'t about more being better — it has to match your body\'s ability to recover. Beginners should do 3 full-body sessions a week (e.g. Mon/Wed/Fri), covering the big muscle groups each time; advanced lifters can use an upper/lower split 4 days a week for higher volume per muscle group. Frequency matters more than per-session volume: the muscle protein synthesis signal peaks 24-48 hours after training, so only regular stimulation keeps you growing. Don\'t leave more than 72 hours between sessions for the same muscle group, or the signal fades and long-term progress suffers.',
  '训练频率与分化': 'Training Frequency and Split',
  '训练频率偏高': 'High Training Frequency',
  '训练频率过低（每周仅1次）使肌蛋白合成窗口未被充分利用，可考虑将手臂拆分到推拉日': 'Training frequency too low (only once a week) leaves the muscle protein synthesis window underused — consider moving arm work onto push/pull days',
  '训练频率过高导致中枢神经系统疲劳，表现为睡眠质量下降与训练表现退步': 'Excessively high training frequency causes central nervous system fatigue, which shows up as poorer sleep quality and declining performance',
  '训练频率过高（>3次/周）或单次容量过大（>10组/肌群）导致恢复不足反而影响生长': 'Training frequency too high (>3 sessions/week) or per-session volume too large (>10 sets/muscle group) causes under-recovery and actually hinders growth',
  '训练频率：新手建议每周3次，全身训练或上下肢分化。\n\n训练容量：每个动作3-4组，每组8-12次，组间休息60-90秒。\n\n渐进超负荷：每周尝试增加重量或次数，记录训练日志追踪进步。\n\n动作选择：以复合动作（深蹲、卧推、硬拉、引体）为主，孤立动作为辅。\n\n热身：5分钟轻度有氧 + 动态拉伸；放松：5分钟静态拉伸。': 'Training frequency: beginners should aim for 3 sessions a week, either full-body or an upper/lower split.\n\nTraining volume: 3-4 sets per exercise, 8-12 reps per set, 60-90 seconds rest between sets.\n\nProgressive overload: try to add weight or reps every week and log your workouts to track progress.\n\nExercise selection: prioritize compound lifts (squat, bench press, deadlift, pull-up) with isolation work as support.\n\nWarm-up: 5 minutes of light cardio plus dynamic stretching; cool-down: 5 minutes of static stretching.',
  '训练频率：每周2-3次（腹直肌需48小时恢复），每次8-12分钟复合训练，DOMS属正常适应': 'Training frequency: 2-3 times a week (the rectus abdominis needs 48 hours to recover), 8-12 minutes of compound work each session; DOMS is a normal adaptation',
