  '骨盆中立，下背贴地，肩胛微离地准备，核心激活，颈部放松不紧张，目视上方方向。': 'Keep the pelvis neutral and the lower back pressed into the floor, lift the shoulder blades slightly to get set, activate the core, keep the neck relaxed rather than tense, and look upward.',
  '髋部后坐同时屈膝下蹲，膝盖沿脚尖方向，背部保持中立，下蹲过程吸气，重心保持在足中位置。': 'Sit the hips back while bending the knees into the squat, knees tracking in line with the toes, back neutral, inhale on the way down, and keep your weight over the midfoot.',
  '髋部后坐屈膝': 'Sit hips back and bend knees',
  '髋部铰链俯身': 'Hinge at the hips to lean forward',
  '髋部铰链前倾约45度，背部保持中立': 'Hinge at the hips into about 45 degrees of forward lean with your back neutral',
  '髋部铰链后推，膝盖微屈': 'Hinge at the hips, knees slightly bent',
  '髋部铰链启动，保持背部中立': 'Initiate with a hip hinge, keeping your back neutral',
  '高位': 'High Pulley',
  '高位下拉': 'Lat Pulldown',
  '高位下拉模拟引体向上动作，适合无法完成引体向上的训练者。': 'The lat pulldown mimics the pull-up movement, making it suitable for trainees who can\'t yet do a pull-up.',
  '高位下拉：主练背阔肌，下拉过头，是引体向上的入门替代\n坐姿划船：主练中背部与菱形肌，改善含胸驼背\n坐姿下拉/低拉：练下背与核心稳定\n肩推机 / 蝴蝶机后束：练肩部前中束': 'Lat pulldown: primarily targets the lats, pulling down past the head; an entry-level substitute for the pull-up\nSeated row: primarily targets the mid-back and rhomboids, improving rounded shoulders\nSeated pulldown / low row: trains the lower back and core stability\nShoulder press machine / reverse pec deck: trains the front and middle delts',
  '高强度冲刺': 'High-Intensity Sprint',
  '高强度间歇训练': 'High-Intensity Interval Training',
  '高手': 'Advanced',
  '高手教学': 'Advanced Tutorials',
  '高抬腿': 'High Knees',
  '高效减脂训练指南': 'An Efficient Fat-Loss Training Guide',
  '高杠位深蹲：杠铃置于斜方肌上部，双脚与肩同宽，脚尖外展 15-30°。下蹲时膝盖跟踪脚尖方向、髋部同步后移，深度至大腿与地面平行或略低。保持脊柱中立、挺胸、核心加压。站起时同步伸展髋膝，不要先抬臀再起身上身。深蹲的关键是髋膝同步——任何一端先动都会导致杠铃轨迹偏移和力量泄漏。': 'High-bar squat: rest the barbell on the upper traps, feet shoulder-width apart, toes turned out 15-30°. As you descend, let the knees track in line with the toes while the hips shift back, going until the thighs are parallel to the floor or slightly below. Keep the spine neutral, chest up, and core braced. Stand up by extending the hips and knees together — don\'t shoot the hips up first and then lift your chest. The key to squatting is hip-knee synchronization: if either end moves first, the bar path drifts and you leak power.',
  '高级': 'Advanced',
  '高级分化的选择不是看"哪个最有效"，而是看"哪个最适合自己"。推拉腿（PPL）每周 6 次适合恢复能力强者；上下肢每周 4 次适合恢复一般者；六分化每周 6 次适合追求极致专项者；五分化每周 5 次适合传统健美偏好。选择依据：①恢复能力（睡眠、营养、压力）；②训练经验（3 年+ 适合高频率）；③生活方式（工作强度、家庭责任）；④基因（肌肉恢复速度）。盲目模仿他人的分化是高级者最常犯的错误。': 'Choosing an advanced split isn\'t about "which is most effective" but "which fits you best." Push/pull/legs (PPL) 6 days a week suits people with strong recovery; upper/lower 4 days a week suits average recovery; a six-day split suits those chasing maximum specialization; a five-day split suits traditional bodybuilding preferences. Decide based on: ① recovery capacity (sleep, nutrition, stress); ② training experience (3+ years fits higher frequency); ③ lifestyle (work intensity, family responsibilities); ④ genetics (muscle recovery speed). Blindly copying someone else\'s split is the most common mistake advanced lifters make.',
  '高级分化的选择依据': 'How to Choose an Advanced Split',
  '高级分化：推拉腿/上下肢/六分化，按个体恢复能力选择。\n\n个体化原则：基因/恢复/经验/生活方式决定最优方案。\n\n长期规划：每年 2-3 个中周期，每个聚焦不同目标。': 'Advanced splits: push/pull/legs, upper/lower, or a six-day split, chosen based on individual recovery capacity.\n\nIndividualization principle: genetics / recovery / experience / lifestyle determine the optimal plan.\n\nLong-term planning: 2-3 mesocycles per year, each focused on a different goal.',
  '高级增肌突破': 'Advanced Hypertrophy Breakthrough',
  '高级增肌者应有年度规划，每年 4 个中周期（每个 12-16 周），每个中周期聚焦不同目标。例如：Q1 力量保留期（强度主导 80-85% 1RM）、Q2 肌肥大突破期（容量主导 18-22 组/周）、Q3 代谢压力期（高次数+超级组）、Q4 综合整合期（均衡容量与强度）。每个中周期结束后 deload 1-2 周，评估体成分与力量数据，调整下个中周期。这种年度规划让训练有长期方向，避免无目的的随机训练。增肌是 5-10 年的工程，年度规划是导航。': 'Advanced muscle builders should plan by the year: 4 mesocycles per year (12-16 weeks each), each focused on a different goal. For example: Q1 strength maintenance (intensity-led, 80-85% 1RM), Q2 hypertrophy breakthrough (volume-led, 18-22 sets/week), Q3 metabolic stress (high reps + supersets), Q4 integration (balanced volume and intensity). After each mesocycle, deload for 1-2 weeks, review body composition and strength data, then adjust the next one. This kind of annual planning gives training long-term direction and avoids aimless, random workouts. Building muscle is a 5-10 year project, and annual planning is your navigation.',
  '高级瓶颈的 90% 是恢复不足，不是训练不够。出现力量退步、睡眠变差、晨起心率上升，立即 deload': '90% of advanced plateaus come from under-recovery, not under-training. If your strength drops, your sleep worsens, or your morning heart rate rises, deload immediately',
  '高级瓶颈：肌肉量停滞、围度无变化、训练表现平台。\n\n诊断维度：容量/强度/频率/营养/恢复/动作选择。\n\n关键指标：单肌群周容量、训练日志趋势、体成分变化。': 'Advanced plateau: muscle mass stalled, measurements unchanged, performance flat.\n\nDiagnostic dimensions: volume / intensity / frequency / nutrition / recovery / exercise selection.\n\nKey metrics: weekly volume per muscle group, training log trends, body composition changes.',
  '高级者每 12 周评估一次分化方案。如果连续 2 个月进步停滞，先尝试切换分化（如 PPL→上下肢）再考虑其他调整': 'Advanced lifters should reassess their split every 12 weeks. If progress stalls for 2 straight months, first try switching splits (e.g. PPL → upper/lower) before considering other changes',
  '高级训练者必须有完整的训练日志，包括每个动作的重量、组数、次数、RPE。趋势分析比单次数据更重要：连续 4 周主项 RPE 上升但重量不变 = 容量过度；连续 6 周重量无突破 = 需要动作变式；连续 8 周围度无变化 = 营养或恢复出问题。没有日志的"感觉停滞"是主观的，无法指导调整。日志是高级训练者的"X 光片"。': 'Advanced lifters must keep a complete training log, including weight, sets, reps, and RPE for every exercise. Trend analysis matters more than any single data point: main lift RPE rising for 4 straight weeks with weight unchanged = too much volume; no weight progress for 6 straight weeks = you need exercise variation; no measurement change for 8 straight weeks = a nutrition or recovery problem. "Feeling stuck" without a log is subjective and can\'t guide adjustments. The log is an advanced lifter\'s "X-ray".',
  '高级训练者的瓶颈与初学者完全不同。初学者的瓶颈是"不够练"，高级者的瓶颈是"恢复跟不上"+"刺激不够新"。1.5 年以上训练者肌肉蛋白合成对训练的响应降低 30-50%，同样的训练容量产生的增长效应减弱。这就是为什么高级者需要更精细的周期化、更新的动作刺激、更严格的恢复管理——而不是简单加量。盲目加量在高级阶段只会导致过度训练。': 'An advanced trainee\'s plateau is completely different from a beginner\'s. A beginner\'s bottleneck is "not training enough"; an advanced lifter\'s is "recovery can\'t keep up" plus "the stimulus isn\'t new enough." After 1.5+ years of training, the muscle protein synthesis response to training drops 30-50%, so the same training volume produces less growth. That\'s why advanced lifters need finer periodization, fresher exercise stimuli, and stricter recovery management — not simply more volume. Blindly adding volume at the advanced stage only leads to overtraining.',
  '高级训练者的身体适应速度极快，连续 4 周以上使用相同容量与强度必然进入平台。周期化通过有计划的累加与减量交替，让身体在累加周接受新刺激、在减量周超量恢复，实现螺旋式进步。肌肥大周期化的核心是"容量累加 + 强度波动 + 定期减量"，与力量周期化（强度主导）不同。高级者脱离周期化谈增肌，等于在适应曲线上原地踏步。': 'Advanced trainees adapt extremely fast, so using the same volume and intensity for more than 4 straight weeks guarantees a plateau. Periodization alternates planned accumulation with deloads, so the body takes on new stimulus during accumulation weeks and supercompensates during deload weeks, producing spiral-shaped progress. The core of hypertrophy periodization is "volume accumulation + intensity variation + regular deloads," which differs from strength periodization (intensity-led). For an advanced lifter, chasing hypertrophy without periodization means standing still on the adaptation curve.',
  '高频率恢复管理：每日睡眠7-9小时，蛋白质摄入1.8-2.2g/kg体重，训练后及时补充碳水+蛋白': 'Recovery management for high frequency: 7-9 hours of sleep a day, 1.8-2.2 g/kg body weight of protein, and carbs + protein promptly after training',
  '鸟狗式': 'Bird-Dog',
  '鸡胸肉（每 100g 31g 蛋白、165 大卡）是减脂期性价比之王，便宜、易得、好烹饪。鱼虾低脂高蛋白，三文鱼虽脂肪略高但富含 Omega-3，能降低炎症、改善胰岛素敏感性。鸡蛋清是纯蛋白质零碳水的代表，一个蛋清约 3.6g 蛋白。瘦牛肉富含肌酸和铁，适合训练量大的人。希腊酸奶是加餐首选，蛋白含量是普通酸奶的 2-3 倍。': 'Chicken breast (31 g protein and 165 kcal per 100 g) is the best value of any fat-loss food — cheap, easy to find, and easy to cook. Fish and shrimp are low in fat and high in protein; salmon is a bit higher in fat but rich in Omega-3s, which reduce inflammation and improve insulin sensitivity. Egg whites are the classic pure-protein, zero-carb choice at about 3.6 g of protein each. Lean beef is rich in creatine and iron, good for people with high training volume. Greek yogurt is the top pick for a snack, with 2-3 times the protein of regular yogurt.',
